{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:56:49.876Z","ordinal":10558,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a5d9f2c9487d0a51c789f69710660","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Copilot 1.0.82 gives us a better token source than expected: `session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is keyed by the child UUID and contains the full input/output/cache/API-call breakdown, so we can populate the existing `TokenUsage` contract accurately.\n- File attribution is also deterministic through `parentToolCallId`; however, current Copilot emits `filePaths` under `restrictedProperties`, while the existing parser only reads `properties`. I’ll extend the shared extractor once, then filter it by the matched parent task ID.\n- The native start hook is intentionally not sufficient for correlation: two simultaneous starts were byte-for-byte identical. The implementation must treat the stop hook plus transcript as authoritative instead of guessing by timestamp or agent name.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788501407232,"completed_at_ms":1788501409876}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:56:49.880Z","ordinal":10559,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a5d9f2c9487d0a51c789f69710660","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Copilot 1.0.82 gives us a better token source than expected: `session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is keyed by the child UUID and contains the full input/output/cache/API-call breakdown, so we can populate the existing `TokenUsage` contract accurately.\n- File attribution is also deterministic through `parentToolCallId`; however, current Copilot emits `filePaths` under `restrictedProperties`, while the existing parser only reads `properties`. I’ll extend the shared extractor once, then filter it by the matched parent task ID.\n- The native start hook is intentionally not sufficient for correlation: two simultaneous starts were byte-for-byte identical. The implementation must treat the stop hook plus transcript as authoritative instead of guessing by timestamp or agent name.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788501404.201861,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
