{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:35:01.750Z","ordinal":10952,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a749d218c87d0b3b71901d7d29065","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4tbpYPIzikNgCc5jd19cxO4z","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\\n@@\\n-Copilot CLI has a complete hook system with 8 hook types, JSONL transcripts, and session management. All required lifecycle events map cleanly.\\n+Copilot CLI has a complete hook system with 9 hook types, JSONL transcripts, and session management. All required lifecycle events map cleanly.\\n@@\\n-| Version info | PASS | `0.0.420` |\\n-| Hook keywords | PASS | 8 hook types in `.github/hooks/*.json` |\\n+| Version info | PASS | Native subagent contract verified with `1.0.82` |\\n+| Hook keywords | PASS | 9 hook types in `.github/hooks/*.json` |\\n@@\\n-- Version: `0.0.420` (GA as of 2026-02-25)\\n+- Verified version: `1.0.82`\\n@@\\n | `sessionEnd` | Session completed/terminated | `timestamp`, `cwd`, `sessionId`, `reason` | `SessionEnd` |\\n-| `subagentStop` | Subagent finishes | `timestamp`, `cwd`, `sessionId`, *(TBD — needs capture)* | `SubagentEnd` |\\n+| `subagentStart` | Subagent starts | parent `sessionId`/`transcriptPath`, agent name | pass-through; payload has no child identity |\\n+| `subagentStop` | Subagent finishes | parent `sessionId`/`transcriptPath`, child `agentId`, `agentType`, `agentName` | correlated `SubagentEnd` |\\n@@\\n-- `tool.execution_complete` — Tool result (`toolCallId`, `toolTelemetry.properties.filePaths` (JSON-encoded string array), `linesAdded`, `linesRemoved`)\\n+- `tool.execution_complete` — Tool result (`toolCallId`, `parentToolCallId`, top-level `agentId`, and JSON-encoded `filePaths` under `toolTelemetry.properties` or `restrictedProperties`)\\n+- `subagent.started` — Stable join between top-level child `agentId` and the parent task `toolCallId`\\n+- `subagent.completed` — Completion totals, written after the synchronous `subagentStop` hook returns\\n@@\\n-The `assistant.message` entries have a `toolRequests` array with tool call IDs. After each tool executes, a `tool.execution_complete` event is emitted with `toolTelemetry.properties.filePaths`, where `filePaths` is a string containing a JSON array of file paths modified by that tool call. The `TranscriptAnalyzer` implementation parses this `filePaths` property to extract modified files for checkpoint metadata.\\n+The `assistant.message` entries have a `toolRequests` array with tool call IDs. After each tool executes, a `tool.execution_complete` event is emitted with a JSON-encoded `filePaths` value. Current releases place sensitive telemetry under `restrictedProperties`; older fixtures use `properties`, so the parser supports both.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788507291.895871}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:35:01.848Z","ordinal":10953,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-382261d5-5b6f-4ee5-a927-842a3008c455","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -4,3 +4,3 @@\n \n-Copilot CLI has a complete hook system with 8 hook types, JSONL transcripts, and session management. All required lifecycle events map cleanly.\n+Copilot CLI has a complete hook system with 9 hook types, JSONL transcripts, and session management. All required lifecycle events map cleanly.\n \n@@ -12,4 +12,4 @@\n | Help available | PASS | Full `--help` with subcommands |\n-| Version info | PASS | `0.0.420` |\n-| Hook keywords | PASS | 8 hook types in `.github/hooks/*.json` |\n+| Version info | PASS | Native subagent contract verified with `1.0.82` |\n+| Hook keywords | PASS | 9 hook types in `.github/hooks/*.json` |\n | Session keywords | PASS | `--resume`, `--continue`, `--share` |\n@@ -21,3 +21,3 @@\n - Name: `copilot`\n-- Version: `0.0.420` (GA as of 2026-02-25)\n+- Verified version: `1.0.82`\n - Install: `brew install copilot-cli` or `npm install -g @github/copilot`\n@@ -57,3 +57,4 @@\n | `sessionEnd` | Session completed/terminated | `timestamp`, `cwd`, `sessionId`, `reason` | `SessionEnd` |\n-| `subagentStop` | Subagent finishes | `timestamp`, `cwd`, `sessionId`, *(TBD — needs capture)* | `SubagentEnd` |\n+| `subagentStart` | Subagent starts | parent `sessionId`/`transcriptPath`, agent name | pass-through; payload has no child identity |\n+| `subagentStop` | Subagent finishes | parent `sessionId`/`transcriptPath`, child `agentId`, `agentType`, `agentName` | correlated `SubagentEnd` |\n | `preToolUse` | Before tool execution | *(TBD — needs capture)* | *(pass-through)* |\n@@ -104,3 +105,5 @@\n - `assistant.message` — Assistant response (`content`, `toolRequests[]`, `reasoningText`)\n-- `tool.execution_complete` — Tool result (`toolCallId`, `toolTelemetry.properties.filePaths` (JSON-encoded string array), `linesAdded`, `linesRemoved`)\n+- `tool.execution_complete` — Tool result (`toolCallId`, `parentToolCallId`, top-level `agentId`, and JSON-encoded `filePaths` under `toolTelemetry.properties` or `restrictedProperties`)\n+- `subagent.started` — Stable join between top-level child `agentId` and the parent task `toolCallId`\n+- `subagent.completed` — Completion totals, written after the synchronous `subagentStop` hook returns\n - `assistant.turn_end` — End of assistant turn (`turnId`)\n@@ -118,3 +121,3 @@\n \n-The `assistant.message` entries have a `toolRequests` array with tool call IDs. After each tool executes, a `tool.execution_complete` event is emitted with `toolTelemetry.properties.filePaths`, where `filePaths` is a string containing a JSON array of file paths modified by that tool call. The `TranscriptAnalyzer` implementation parses this `filePaths` property to extract modified files for checkpoint metadata.\n+The `assistant.message` entries have a `toolRequests` array with tool call IDs. After each tool executes, a `tool.execution_complete` event is emitted with a JSON-encoded `filePaths` value. Current releases place sensitive telemetry under `restrictedProperties`; older fixtures use `properties`, so the parser supports both.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788507301791,"completed_at_ms":1788507301848}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:35:01.903Z","ordinal":10954,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a06b57-a80f-7b53-9ded-4e95f1a114ce","call_id":"call_4tbpYPIzikNgCc5jd19cxO4z","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788507301.903552}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:35:01.904Z","ordinal":10955,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":210620732,"cached_input_tokens":207089152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":568744,"reasoning_output_tokens":204832,"total_tokens":211189476},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":172384,"cached_input_tokens":171392,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":722,"reasoning_output_tokens":13,"total_tokens":173106},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":100.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1788886333},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":null},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"self_serve_business_prolite","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:35:14.047Z","ordinal":10956,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a74a85bf887d0b8cb3c6bb2fa4394","status":"completed","call_id":"call_rj13SmGklQpcRFmKKsERF7Z1","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\\n@@\\n ## Subagent Lifecycle\\n \\n-Copilot CLI has **one-sided** subagent hooks: `subagentStop` fires but `subagentStart` does NOT\\n-(tested by registering the hook — Copilot CLI ignores it). The transcript does contain\\n-`subagent.started` / `subagent.completed` events with `toolCallId`, but these are not\\n-surfaced as hooks.\\n-\\n-The `preToolUse` / `postToolUse` hooks fire with `toolName: \\\"task\\\"` for subagent lifecycle,\\n-which could be used as an alternative mechanism for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd` in the future.\\n-\\n-Because there is no `SubagentStart` hook, the framework cannot capture pre-task state (untracked\\n-files snapshot). The `handleLifecycleSubagentEnd` dispatcher falls back to the session's\\n-pre-prompt state to avoid spurious task checkpoints from pre-existing untracked files\\n-(e.g., `.github/hooks/entire.json`).\\n+Copilot CLI 1.0.82 emits both native hooks for custom agents and the built-in\\n+`general-purpose` agent. `subagentStart` names the parent session and agent type but\\n+does not expose a child ID or task call ID; two concurrent same-type starts can be\\n+identical, so Entire deliberately treats it as pass-through.\\n+\\n+At true completion, `subagentStop` adds the child UUID as `agentId`. Before invoking\\n+that hook, Copilot has already written `subagent.started` to the parent\\n+`events.jsonl`; that event carries the same top-level child UUID and the stable parent\\n+task `toolCallId`. Entire reads the parent transcript through `SessionStore` and joins\\n+on the UUID. Child tool events carry the same UUID plus `parentToolCallId`, allowing\\n+two concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\\n+\\n+Copilot does not create standalone child transcript files. Task metadata therefore\\n+records transcript unavailability and never probes the generic Claude-style\\n+`agent-<id>.jsonl` layout. Per-child token breakdown is also unavailable at hook time:\\n+`session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is authoritative but is appended only after\\n+`sessionEnd` returns. Entire leaves child token usage unset rather than misclassifying\\n+Copilot's total-only completion value.\\n@@\\n-- No `SubagentStart` hook — only `subagentStop` fires; framework falls back to pre-prompt state\\n-- `subagentStop` payload fields beyond `timestamp`/`cwd`/`sessionId` not yet fully captured\\n-- `preToolUse` / `postToolUse` payloads not yet leveraged (could provide SubagentStart equivalent)\\n-- Tool request schema in transcripts needs verification with a real tool-using session\\n+- No standalone child transcript; Copilot interleaves child events into the parent JSONL\\n+- Exact per-child token breakdown becomes available only after the last synchronous hook\\n+- `subagentStart` cannot be correlated safely and is retained as an observed pass-through hook\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788507303.49295}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:35:14.149Z","ordinal":10957,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-90e8b2f2-f251-4c77-b67f-30153df3feb8","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -205,14 +205,20 @@\n \n-Copilot CLI has **one-sided** subagent hooks: `subagentStop` fires but `subagentStart` does NOT\n-(tested by registering the hook — Copilot CLI ignores it). The transcript does contain\n-`subagent.started` / `subagent.completed` events with `toolCallId`, but these are not\n-surfaced as hooks.\n+Copilot CLI 1.0.82 emits both native hooks for custom agents and the built-in\n+`general-purpose` agent. `subagentStart` names the parent session and agent type but\n+does not expose a child ID or task call ID; two concurrent same-type starts can be\n+identical, so Entire deliberately treats it as pass-through.\n \n-The `preToolUse` / `postToolUse` hooks fire with `toolName: \"task\"` for subagent lifecycle,\n-which could be used as an alternative mechanism for `SubagentStart`/`SubagentEnd` in the future.\n+At true completion, `subagentStop` adds the child UUID as `agentId`. Before invoking\n+that hook, Copilot has already written `subagent.started` to the parent\n+`events.jsonl`; that event carries the same top-level child UUID and the stable parent\n+task `toolCallId`. Entire reads the parent transcript through `SessionStore` and joins\n+on the UUID. Child tool events carry the same UUID plus `parentToolCallId`, allowing\n+two concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\n \n-Because there is no `SubagentStart` hook, the framework cannot capture pre-task state (untracked\n-files snapshot). The `handleLifecycleSubagentEnd` dispatcher falls back to the session's\n-pre-prompt state to avoid spurious task checkpoints from pre-existing untracked files\n-(e.g., `.github/hooks/entire.json`).\n+Copilot does not create standalone child transcript files. Task metadata therefore\n+records transcript unavailability and never probes the generic Claude-style\n+`agent-<id>.jsonl` layout. Per-child token breakdown is also unavailable at hook time:\n+`session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is authoritative but is appended only after\n+`sessionEnd` returns. Entire leaves child token usage unset rather than misclassifying\n+Copilot's total-only completion value.\n \n@@ -221,6 +227,5 @@\n - No `Compaction` event — Copilot CLI doesn't appear to have a context compaction hook\n-- No `SubagentStart` hook — only `subagentStop` fires; framework falls back to pre-prompt state\n-- `subagentStop` payload fields beyond `timestamp`/`cwd`/`sessionId` not yet fully captured\n-- `preToolUse` / `postToolUse` payloads not yet leveraged (could provide SubagentStart equivalent)\n-- Tool request schema in transcripts needs verification with a real tool-using session\n+- No standalone child transcript; Copilot interleaves child events into the parent JSONL\n+- Exact per-child token breakdown becomes available only after the last synchronous hook\n+- `subagentStart` cannot be correlated safely and is retained as an observed pass-through hook\n - `transcriptPath` only available in `agentStop` hook — `userPromptSubmitted` and `sessionStart` don't include it, so we compute it from `~/.copilot/session-state/<sessionId>/events.jsonl`\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788507314093,"completed_at_ms":1788507314149}}
