{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:37:22.609Z","ordinal":10973,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":211142422,"cached_input_tokens":207607936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":570570,"reasoning_output_tokens":205018,"total_tokens":211712992},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":174658,"cached_input_tokens":173696,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":346,"reasoning_output_tokens":148,"total_tokens":175004},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":100.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1788886333},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":null},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"self_serve_business_prolite","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:55:20.204Z","ordinal":10974,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":211142422,"cached_input_tokens":207607936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":570570,"reasoning_output_tokens":205018,"total_tokens":211712992},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":174658,"cached_input_tokens":173696,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":346,"reasoning_output_tokens":148,"total_tokens":175004},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":100.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1788886333},"secondary":null,"credits":{"has_credits":true,"unlimited":false,"balance":null},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"self_serve_business_prolite","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:05:24.743Z","ordinal":10975,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a796b473487d0bcab914fbd9f66dc","status":"completed","call_id":"call_C2U0WuJRM85Z4gPhG77wbn6y","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md\\n+# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\\n+\\n+## Goal\\n+\\n+Give GitHub Copilot CLI durable, per-child task tracking using the shared Entire\\n+subagent record and checkpoint format. Concurrent children must remain distinct,\\n+read-only children must still produce records, and ambiguous evidence must fail\\n+closed rather than merge children together.\\n+\\n+## Verified Copilot contract\\n+\\n+The contract was captured from the official Copilot CLI 1.0.82 release in an\\n+isolated repository. Three paid evidence invocations covered:\\n+\\n+- two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one read-only; and\\n+- the built-in `general-purpose` child.\\n+\\n+Both custom and built-in children emit `subagentStart` and `subagentStop`.\\n+The start payload contains the parent session ID, parent transcript path, and\\n+agent name, but no child UUID or task call ID. Two concurrent starts can be\\n+identical, so start cannot safely create a keyed record.\\n+\\n+The stop payload contains:\\n+\\n+- the parent UUID as `sessionId`;\\n+- the parent `events.jsonl` as `transcriptPath`;\\n+- the child UUID as `agentId`; and\\n+- `agentType` and `agentName`.\\n+\\n+Before the stop hook runs, the parent transcript contains a `subagent.started`\\n+event with the same top-level child UUID and the parent task `toolCallId`.\\n+Child tool events carry the same top-level child UUID and a\\n+`parentToolCallId` equal to that task ID. This is a deterministic join for\\n+concurrent children and does not depend on descriptions, timestamps, ordering,\\n+or response text.\\n+\\n+Copilot stores all child events in the parent transcript; no standalone child\\n+transcript exists. `subagent.completed` is appended only after the synchronous\\n+stop hook returns. Full per-child token breakdown appears later in\\n+`session.shutdown.agentMetrics`, after the synchronous `sessionEnd` hook\\n+returns. The adapter therefore cannot honestly attach the child transcript or\\n+exact token breakdown while handling the child completion.\\n+\\n+## Design\\n+\\n+### Hooks and upgrades\\n+\\n+Entire installs all nine Copilot hook commands, including `subagentStart` and\\n+`subagentStop`. `subagentStart` is parsed as an observed pass-through signal\\n+because it lacks a stable child identity. `subagentStop` drives durable capture.\\n+\\n+Copilot implements hook freshness reporting. A repository with any Entire-owned\\n+Copilot hook but without the full current command set is outdated, so an older\\n+eight-hook installation is surfaced and a reinstall adds exactly the missing\\n+start hook while preserving user hooks and unknown fields.\\n+\\n+### Stop correlation\\n+\\n+On `subagentStop`, the adapter:\\n+\\n+1. opens Copilot's session store through `agent.SessionStore`;\\n+2. verifies that `transcriptPath` is exactly the expected\\n+   `<parent-session>/events.jsonl` beneath that store;\\n+3. reads it with the rooted no-follow API;\\n+4. finds the unique `subagent.started` whose top-level `agentId` matches the\\n+   stop payload; and\\n+5. uses its `data.toolCallId` as Entire's `ToolUseID`.\\n+\\n+Zero or multiple identities produce no normalized event. The adapter does not\\n+fall back to parsing task result text.\\n+\\n+The child file list is the deduplicated `filePaths` from\\n+`tool.execution_complete` events whose top-level child UUID matches and whose\\n+`parentToolCallId` equals the correlated task ID. Both the older\\n+`toolTelemetry.properties` and current `restrictedProperties` locations are\\n+accepted.\\n+\\n+### Shared lifecycle\\n+\\n+The normalized stop is a true final `SubagentEnd` marked as a correlated\\n+completion learned without a launch marker. Shared lifecycle may create its\\n+task record only if the parent session state already exists and is active.\\n+Missing or ended parent state is a no-op; no session can be resurrected.\\n+\\n+Completion uses only adapter-supplied child files. It skips the whole-worktree\\n+diff and child-transcript analyzer, both of which would over-attribute parent or\\n+concurrent-child activity. The normal exactly-once task-record mutation handles\\n+duplicate stops and preserves one record per `ToolUseID`.\\n+\\n+Each record persists `transcript_unavailable: true`. Condensation still writes\\n+`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` but never probes the generic Claude-style\\n+`agent-<id>.jsonl` fallback. This prevents an unrelated coincidental file from\\n+being attached to the Copilot child.\\n+\\n+### Tokens and transcript\\n+\\n+The task record truthfully reports transcript unavailability and leaves child\\n+token usage unset. `subagent.completed.totalTokens` is exact but cannot be read\\n+until the stop hook returns, and the current `TokenUsage` schema has no\\n+total-only field. Mapping that total to input or output would be incorrect.\\n+\\n+Parent-session transcript and token handling remains unchanged. A future\\n+Copilot hook exposing completed usage, or a future shared total-only token\\n+field, can enrich the same task record without changing correlation.\\n+\\n+## Security and privacy\\n+\\n+- Hook-provided paths are never read with unrestricted `os.ReadFile`.\\n+- Parent transcript reads are confined to Copilot's session store and reject\\n+  outside paths, wrong layouts, and symlinks.\\n+- Unsafe session, task, and child IDs remain covered by central lifecycle\\n+  validation.\\n+- Logs contain operational IDs and errors, never prompts, responses, or file\\n+  contents.\\n+- Evidence fixtures committed to tests contain synthetic structure only.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- A fresh install has one managed start and stop hook; an old install is marked\\n+  outdated and upgrades idempotently.\\n+- Custom and `general-purpose` stops resolve to stable non-empty task IDs.\\n+- Two concurrent same-type children retain disjoint file lists.\\n+- A read-only child still creates a completed task record.\\n+- Duplicate, unmatched, missing-parent, and ended-parent stops create no extra\\n+  record and never resurrect state.\\n+- Condensation writes task metadata and never fabricates a child transcript.\\n+- Existing Copilot parent-session behavior and other agents remain unchanged.\\n+- Focused unit tests, the shared canary, repository checks, and an explicitly\\n+  authorized real Copilot end-user smoke test pass before push.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788508521.789017}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:05:24.814Z","ordinal":10976,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-6dbff050-7c31-4f57-ac97-e9e4a0e88958","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\n\n## Goal\n\nGive GitHub Copilot CLI durable, per-child task tracking using the shared Entire\nsubagent record and checkpoint format. Concurrent children must remain distinct,\nread-only children must still produce records, and ambiguous evidence must fail\nclosed rather than merge children together.\n\n## Verified Copilot contract\n\nThe contract was captured from the official Copilot CLI 1.0.82 release in an\nisolated repository. Three paid evidence invocations covered:\n\n- two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one read-only; and\n- the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n\nBoth custom and built-in children emit `subagentStart` and `subagentStop`.\nThe start payload contains the parent session ID, parent transcript path, and\nagent name, but no child UUID or task call ID. Two concurrent starts can be\nidentical, so start cannot safely create a keyed record.\n\nThe stop payload contains:\n\n- the parent UUID as `sessionId`;\n- the parent `events.jsonl` as `transcriptPath`;\n- the child UUID as `agentId`; and\n- `agentType` and `agentName`.\n\nBefore the stop hook runs, the parent transcript contains a `subagent.started`\nevent with the same top-level child UUID and the parent task `toolCallId`.\nChild tool events carry the same top-level child UUID and a\n`parentToolCallId` equal to that task ID. This is a deterministic join for\nconcurrent children and does not depend on descriptions, timestamps, ordering,\nor response text.\n\nCopilot stores all child events in the parent transcript; no standalone child\ntranscript exists. `subagent.completed` is appended only after the synchronous\nstop hook returns. Full per-child token breakdown appears later in\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics`, after the synchronous `sessionEnd` hook\nreturns. The adapter therefore cannot honestly attach the child transcript or\nexact token breakdown while handling the child completion.\n\n## Design\n\n### Hooks and upgrades\n\nEntire installs all nine Copilot hook commands, including `subagentStart` and\n`subagentStop`. `subagentStart` is parsed as an observed pass-through signal\nbecause it lacks a stable child identity. `subagentStop` drives durable capture.\n\nCopilot implements hook freshness reporting. A repository with any Entire-owned\nCopilot hook but without the full current command set is outdated, so an older\neight-hook installation is surfaced and a reinstall adds exactly the missing\nstart hook while preserving user hooks and unknown fields.\n\n### Stop correlation\n\nOn `subagentStop`, the adapter:\n\n1. opens Copilot's session store through `agent.SessionStore`;\n2. verifies that `transcriptPath` is exactly the expected\n   `<parent-session>/events.jsonl` beneath that store;\n3. reads it with the rooted no-follow API;\n4. finds the unique `subagent.started` whose top-level `agentId` matches the\n   stop payload; and\n5. uses its `data.toolCallId` as Entire's `ToolUseID`.\n\nZero or multiple identities produce no normalized event. The adapter does not\nfall back to parsing task result text.\n\nThe child file list is the deduplicated `filePaths` from\n`tool.execution_complete` events whose top-level child UUID matches and whose\n`parentToolCallId` equals the correlated task ID. Both the older\n`toolTelemetry.properties` and current `restrictedProperties` locations are\naccepted.\n\n### Shared lifecycle\n\nThe normalized stop is a true final `SubagentEnd` marked as a correlated\ncompletion learned without a launch marker. Shared lifecycle may create its\ntask record only if the parent session state already exists and is active.\nMissing or ended parent state is a no-op; no session can be resurrected.\n\nCompletion uses only adapter-supplied child files. It skips the whole-worktree\ndiff and child-transcript analyzer, both of which would over-attribute parent or\nconcurrent-child activity. The normal exactly-once task-record mutation handles\nduplicate stops and preserves one record per `ToolUseID`.\n\nEach record persists `transcript_unavailable: true`. Condensation still writes\n`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` but never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` fallback. This prevents an unrelated coincidental file from\nbeing attached to the Copilot child.\n\n### Tokens and transcript\n\nThe task record truthfully reports transcript unavailability and leaves child\ntoken usage unset. `subagent.completed.totalTokens` is exact but cannot be read\nuntil the stop hook returns, and the current `TokenUsage` schema has no\ntotal-only field. Mapping that total to input or output would be incorrect.\n\nParent-session transcript and token handling remains unchanged. A future\nCopilot hook exposing completed usage, or a future shared total-only token\nfield, can enrich the same task record without changing correlation.\n\n## Security and privacy\n\n- Hook-provided paths are never read with unrestricted `os.ReadFile`.\n- Parent transcript reads are confined to Copilot's session store and reject\n  outside paths, wrong layouts, and symlinks.\n- Unsafe session, task, and child IDs remain covered by central lifecycle\n  validation.\n- Logs contain operational IDs and errors, never prompts, responses, or file\n  contents.\n- Evidence fixtures committed to tests contain synthetic structure only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A fresh install has one managed start and stop hook; an old install is marked\n  outdated and upgrades idempotently.\n- Custom and `general-purpose` stops resolve to stable non-empty task IDs.\n- Two concurrent same-type children retain disjoint file lists.\n- A read-only child still creates a completed task record.\n- Duplicate, unmatched, missing-parent, and ended-parent stops create no extra\n  record and never resurrect state.\n- Condensation writes task metadata and never fabricates a child transcript.\n- Existing Copilot parent-session behavior and other agents remain unchanged.\n- Focused unit tests, the shared canary, repository checks, and an explicitly\n  authorized real Copilot end-user smoke test pass before push.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788509124749,"completed_at_ms":1788509124814}}
