{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:11:33.279Z","ordinal":10985,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9a7d29c01887d0b7c7eb56e7e9c766","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dJfkw4ymCk4I9BPJXDBXWNIU","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\\n+# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\\n+\\n+> Evidence-backed revision after real Copilot CLI 1.0.82 capture. Keep the\\n+> implementation near 450–700 additions and reuse shared task persistence.\\n+\\n+## 1. Capture the native contract\\n+\\n+- [x] Verify the official current Copilot release and isolate its home/cache.\\n+- [x] Run two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one\\n+  read-only.\\n+- [x] Run the built-in `general-purpose` child.\\n+- [x] Record structural hook/transcript fields only.\\n+- [x] Prove the child UUID → parent task ID join through the top-level\\n+  `agentId` on `subagent.started`.\\n+- [x] Prove file scoping through child `agentId` plus `parentToolCallId`.\\n+- [x] Confirm no standalone child transcript and that exact breakdown arrives\\n+  only after synchronous hooks finish.\\n+\\n+## 2. Install and detect the complete hook set\\n+\\n+- [x] Add `subagent-start` to `HookNames`, config mapping, and typed config.\\n+- [x] Cover fresh install, idempotency, force reinstall, and uninstall through\\n+  the existing loop-based tests.\\n+- [x] Add freshness detection so an old install missing only the start hook is\\n+  outdated and upgrades by one hook.\\n+\\n+## 3. Correlate stop payloads safely\\n+\\n+- [x] Extend the compatibility envelope with captured child metadata.\\n+- [x] Read the parent transcript through `SessionStore` with exact layout and\\n+  no-follow enforcement.\\n+- [x] Extract the unique task ID from `subagent.started` by child UUID.\\n+- [x] Extract only child-scoped file telemetry, supporting both `properties`\\n+  and `restrictedProperties`.\\n+- [x] Treat uncorrelatable start as pass-through and uncorrelatable stop as a\\n+  no-op.\\n+- [x] Test concurrent same-type children, general-purpose shape, ambiguity,\\n+  outside-store paths, and symlink rejection.\\n+\\n+## 4. Reuse durable task lifecycle\\n+\\n+- [x] Add a narrow normalized marker for completion learned without a launch\\n+  record.\\n+- [x] Permit record creation only inside an existing active parent session.\\n+- [x] Reuse `CompleteTaskRecord` for exactly-once completion.\\n+- [x] Use adapter-supplied files only; skip worktree and transcript scans.\\n+- [x] Persist transcript unavailability and make condensation skip generic\\n+  child-layout fallback.\\n+- [x] Test completion, duplicate stop, missing parent, and no-fallback\\n+  materialization.\\n+\\n+## 5. Strengthen shared end-to-end coverage\\n+\\n+- [x] Seed and commit a Copilot custom-agent fixture before Entire capture.\\n+- [x] Make the shared subagent E2E prompt explicitly delegate to that agent.\\n+- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\\n+- [ ] With separate user authorization, run the paid real Copilot E2E.\\n+\\n+## 6. Documentation and verification\\n+\\n+- [x] Update the Copilot integration notes with the verified 1.0.82 contract.\\n+- [x] Update the agent-guide event matrix.\\n+- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\\n+- [ ] Run `mise run dup` and remove accidental duplication.\\n+- [ ] Run `mise run check` before any commit.\\n+- [ ] Confirm final diff size remains below the redesign threshold.\\n+- [ ] With separate user authorization, run a wrapper-free real end-user smoke\\n+  using the candidate Entire binary and inspect the committed task record.\\n+- [ ] Commit only after local gates pass; push only when authorized, then wait\\n+  for all remote gates. Never merge without explicit approval.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788509480.745046}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T08:11:33.363Z","ordinal":10986,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-d5b0e223-655c-4e24-9d83-a290c8d7228b","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> Evidence-backed revision after real Copilot CLI 1.0.82 capture. Keep the\n> implementation near 450–700 additions and reuse shared task persistence.\n\n## 1. Capture the native contract\n\n- [x] Verify the official current Copilot release and isolate its home/cache.\n- [x] Run two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one\n  read-only.\n- [x] Run the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n- [x] Record structural hook/transcript fields only.\n- [x] Prove the child UUID → parent task ID join through the top-level\n  `agentId` on `subagent.started`.\n- [x] Prove file scoping through child `agentId` plus `parentToolCallId`.\n- [x] Confirm no standalone child transcript and that exact breakdown arrives\n  only after synchronous hooks finish.\n\n## 2. Install and detect the complete hook set\n\n- [x] Add `subagent-start` to `HookNames`, config mapping, and typed config.\n- [x] Cover fresh install, idempotency, force reinstall, and uninstall through\n  the existing loop-based tests.\n- [x] Add freshness detection so an old install missing only the start hook is\n  outdated and upgrades by one hook.\n\n## 3. Correlate stop payloads safely\n\n- [x] Extend the compatibility envelope with captured child metadata.\n- [x] Read the parent transcript through `SessionStore` with exact layout and\n  no-follow enforcement.\n- [x] Extract the unique task ID from `subagent.started` by child UUID.\n- [x] Extract only child-scoped file telemetry, supporting both `properties`\n  and `restrictedProperties`.\n- [x] Treat uncorrelatable start as pass-through and uncorrelatable stop as a\n  no-op.\n- [x] Test concurrent same-type children, general-purpose shape, ambiguity,\n  outside-store paths, and symlink rejection.\n\n## 4. Reuse durable task lifecycle\n\n- [x] Add a narrow normalized marker for completion learned without a launch\n  record.\n- [x] Permit record creation only inside an existing active parent session.\n- [x] Reuse `CompleteTaskRecord` for exactly-once completion.\n- [x] Use adapter-supplied files only; skip worktree and transcript scans.\n- [x] Persist transcript unavailability and make condensation skip generic\n  child-layout fallback.\n- [x] Test completion, duplicate stop, missing parent, and no-fallback\n  materialization.\n\n## 5. Strengthen shared end-to-end coverage\n\n- [x] Seed and commit a Copilot custom-agent fixture before Entire capture.\n- [x] Make the shared subagent E2E prompt explicitly delegate to that agent.\n- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run the paid real Copilot E2E.\n\n## 6. Documentation and verification\n\n- [x] Update the Copilot integration notes with the verified 1.0.82 contract.\n- [x] Update the agent-guide event matrix.\n- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` and remove accidental duplication.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check` before any commit.\n- [ ] Confirm final diff size remains below the redesign threshold.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run a wrapper-free real end-user smoke\n  using the candidate Entire binary and inspect the committed task record.\n- [ ] Commit only after local gates pass; push only when authorized, then wait\n  for all remote gates. Never merge without explicit approval.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788509493290,"completed_at_ms":1788509493363}}
