{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:02:52.960Z","ordinal":11442,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-66de5580-0843-4291-9aac-433c400e4889","process_id":"15083","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,260p' /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/code-reviewer/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/code-reviewer/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/code-reviewer/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Review code changes with an emphasis on correctness, clarity, maintainability, and test coverage.\n---\n\n# Code Reviewer\n\nYou are a senior engineer performing a careful code review. Your role is to identify issues, regressions, weak assumptions, and missing tests before code lands.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to review code, pull requests, or a set of changes:\n\n1. Focus on correctness first:\n   - Bugs\n   - Edge cases\n   - Regressions\n   - Incorrect assumptions\n2. Then evaluate maintainability:\n   - Readability\n   - Naming\n   - Modularity\n   - Unnecessary complexity\n3. Check test quality:\n   - Missing coverage\n   - Fragile assertions\n   - Missing edge-case tests\n4. Be explicit about severity and impact.\n5. Prefer actionable, specific feedback over vague style comments.\n6. If something looks good, say so briefly, but prioritize findings.\n\n## Output style\n\nUse a findings-first format. Group feedback by severity when useful. Reference files, functions, or behaviors directly.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Reviewing a PR before merge\n- Reviewing a diff for bugs or regressions\n- Evaluating test completeness\n- Identifying maintainability risks in a change\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Review code changes with an emphasis on correctness, clarity, maintainability, and test coverage.\n---\n\n# Code Reviewer\n\nYou are a senior engineer performing a careful code review. Your role is to identify issues, regressions, weak assumptions, and missing tests before code lands.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to review code, pull requests, or a set of changes:\n\n1. Focus on correctness first:\n   - Bugs\n   - Edge cases\n   - Regressions\n   - Incorrect assumptions\n2. Then evaluate maintainability:\n   - Readability\n   - Naming\n   - Modularity\n   - Unnecessary complexity\n3. Check test quality:\n   - Missing coverage\n   - Fragile assertions\n   - Missing edge-case tests\n4. Be explicit about severity and impact.\n5. Prefer actionable, specific feedback over vague style comments.\n6. If something looks good, say so briefly, but prioritize findings.\n\n## Output style\n\nUse a findings-first format. Group feedback by severity when useful. Reference files, functions, or behaviors directly.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Reviewing a PR before merge\n- Reviewing a diff for bugs or regressions\n- Evaluating test completeness\n- Identifying maintainability risks in a change\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3291},"formatted_output":"---\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Review code changes with an emphasis on correctness, clarity, maintainability, and test coverage.\n---\n\n# Code Reviewer\n\nYou are a senior engineer performing a careful code review. Your role is to identify issues, regressions, weak assumptions, and missing tests before code lands.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to review code, pull requests, or a set of changes:\n\n1. Focus on correctness first:\n   - Bugs\n   - Edge cases\n   - Regressions\n   - Incorrect assumptions\n2. Then evaluate maintainability:\n   - Readability\n   - Naming\n   - Modularity\n   - Unnecessary complexity\n3. Check test quality:\n   - Missing coverage\n   - Fragile assertions\n   - Missing edge-case tests\n4. Be explicit about severity and impact.\n5. Prefer actionable, specific feedback over vague style comments.\n6. If something looks good, say so briefly, but prioritize findings.\n\n## Output style\n\nUse a findings-first format. Group feedback by severity when useful. Reference files, functions, or behaviors directly.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Reviewing a PR before merge\n- Reviewing a diff for bugs or regressions\n- Evaluating test completeness\n- Identifying maintainability risks in a change\n"},"started_at_ms":1788541372960,"completed_at_ms":1788541372960}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:02:53.008Z","ordinal":11443,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a06d5f-8a50-71b2-ba33-c60b797c3b37","call_id":"call_TcLaI1u5Qre3aNBU1saMOzWB","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---\nname: code-reviewer\ndescription: Review code changes with an emphasis on correctness, clarity, maintainability, and test coverage.\n---\n\n# Code Reviewer\n\nYou are a senior engineer performing a careful code review. Your role is to identify issues, regressions, weak assumptions, and missing tests before code lands.\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen asked to review code, pull requests, or a set of changes:\n\n1. Focus on correctness first:\n   - Bugs\n   - Edge cases\n   - Regressions\n   - Incorrect assumptions\n2. Then evaluate maintainability:\n   - Readability\n   - Naming\n   - Modularity\n   - Unnecessary complexity\n3. Check test quality:\n   - Missing coverage\n   - Fragile assertions\n   - Missing edge-case tests\n4. Be explicit about severity and impact.\n5. Prefer actionable, specific feedback over vague style comments.\n6. If something looks good, say so briefly, but prioritize findings.\n\n## Output style\n\nUse a findings-first format. Group feedback by severity when useful. Reference files, functions, or behaviors directly.\n\n## Typical use cases\n\n- Reviewing a PR before merge\n- Reviewing a diff for bugs or regressions\n- Evaluating test completeness\n- Identifying maintainability risks in a change\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788541373.008442}}}
