{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:09:06.050Z","ordinal":11595,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afb2fb7d487d08bd4fb999d6d02d0","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m continuing from the completed implementation and evidence capture. I’m at the closure phase now: finish the duplication check, do one inline full-diff review, then run the repository-required lint/check suite. I won’t launch any subagents or run another paid real-agent test without separate authorization.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe Copilot integration’s key design constraint is timing: the stop hook arrives before the transcript’s completion event, so the reliable join is backward to `subagent.started`, keyed by the child UUID. This avoids races and also keeps concurrent same-type children distinct.\n\nThe other important distinction is “event files” versus a child transcript. Copilot records child work inside the parent JSONL, so the implementation deliberately marks the child transcript unavailable and consumes only the precisely attributed file paths.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788541743735,"completed_at_ms":1788541746050}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:09:06.052Z","ordinal":11596,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afb2fb7d487d08bd4fb999d6d02d0","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’m continuing from the completed implementation and evidence capture. I’m at the closure phase now: finish the duplication check, do one inline full-diff review, then run the repository-required lint/check suite. I won’t launch any subagents or run another paid real-agent test without separate authorization.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe Copilot integration’s key design constraint is timing: the stop hook arrives before the transcript’s completion event, so the reliable join is backward to `subagent.started`, keyed by the child UUID. This avoids races and also keeps concurrent same-type children distinct.\n\nThe other important distinction is “event files” versus a child transcript. Copilot records child work inside the parent JSONL, so the implementation deliberately marks the child transcript unavailable and consumes only the precisely attributed file paths.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788541742.244347,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
