{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:09:33.231Z","ordinal":11623,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016a9afb47c71887d0aec09648e6734a86","status":"completed","call_id":"call_FEdtt5o2KV85i8DH9QLxs9X2","name":"exec","input":"const results = await Promise.all([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff -- cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:20000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff -- cmd/entire/cli/session/state.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_git.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go docs/architecture/agent-guide.md e2e/testutil/repo.go e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:20000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '190,250p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md && sed -n '1,130p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md && sed -n '1,100p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:16000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,220p' mise.toml\",workdir:\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:10000})\n]);\nfor (const r of results) { text(r.output); text(`\\n[exit ${r.exit_code}]\\n`); }","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","create_time":1788541763.00134}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:09:33.305Z","ordinal":11624,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3dd35ffc-5cf4-4c8e-9708-b869192ecb2c","process_id":"96263","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '190,250p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md && sed -n '1,130p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md && sed -n '1,100p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '190,250p' cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md","name":"AGENT.md","path":"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,130p' docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md","name":"2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md","path":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking-design.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,100p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md","name":"2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md","path":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-03-copilot-native-subagent-tracking.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"for the implementation.\n\n## Presence Detection\n\n- No repo-level `.copilot/` directory (unlike other agents)\n- `DetectPresence` delegates to `AreHooksInstalled`, which reads `.github/hooks/entire.json` and checks if any hook entry has an Entire command prefix (`entire ` or `go run \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"/cmd/entire/main.go `)\n- Simply having a `.github/hooks/` directory is NOT sufficient -- the directory must contain `entire.json` with Entire hook entries\n- Alternative: check for `copilot` binary in PATH\n\n## Protected Directories\n\n- `.github/hooks` — the hook config directory; listed in `ProtectedDirs()`, so Entire filters it out of change tracking and checkpoints\n- No agent-specific repo directory to protect\n\n## Subagent Lifecycle\n\nCopilot CLI 1.0.82 emits both native hooks for custom agents and the built-in\n`general-purpose` agent. `subagentStart` names the parent session and agent type but\ndoes not expose a child ID or task call ID; two concurrent same-type starts can be\nidentical, so Entire deliberately treats it as pass-through.\n\nAt true completion, `subagentStop` adds the child UUID as `agentId`. Before invoking\nthat hook, Copilot has already written `subagent.started` to the parent\n`events.jsonl`; that event carries the same top-level child UUID and the stable parent\ntask `toolCallId`. Entire reads the parent transcript through `SessionStore` and joins\non the UUID. Child tool events carry the same UUID plus `parentToolCallId`, allowing\ntwo concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\n\nCopilot does not create standalone child transcript files. Task metadata therefore\nrecords transcript unavailability and never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` layout. Per-child token breakdown is also unavailable at hook time:\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is authoritative but is appended only after\n`sessionEnd` returns. Entire leaves child token usage unset rather than misclassifying\nCopilot's total-only completion value.\n\n## Gaps & Limitations\n\n- No `Compaction` event — Copilot CLI doesn't appear to have a context compaction hook\n- No standalone child transcript; Copilot interleaves child events into the parent JSONL\n- Exact per-child token breakdown becomes available only after the last synchronous hook\n- `subagentStart` cannot be correlated safely and is retained as an observed pass-through hook\n- `transcriptPath` only available in `agentStop` hook — `userPromptSubmitted` and `sessionStart` don't include it, so we compute it from `~/.copilot/session-state/<sessionId>/events.jsonl`\n\n## Captured Payloads\n\n- Contract reverified on 2026-09-03 with Copilot CLI 1.0.82 using two\n  concurrent same-type custom agents (one writing, one read-only) and one\n  built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- Tests retain only synthetic structural fixtures; prompts, responses, and\n  local capture paths are not committed.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\n\n## Goal\n\nGive GitHub Copilot CLI durable, per-child task tracking using the shared Entire\nsubagent record and checkpoint format. Concurrent children must remain distinct,\nread-only children must still produce records, and ambiguous evidence must fail\nclosed rather than merge children together.\n\n## Verified Copilot contract\n\nThe contract was captured from the official Copilot CLI 1.0.82 release in an\nisolated repository. Three paid evidence invocations covered:\n\n- two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one read-only; and\n- the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n\nBoth custom and built-in children emit `subagentStart` and `subagentStop`.\nThe start payload contains the parent session ID, parent transcript path, and\nagent name, but no child UUID or task call ID. Two concurrent starts can be\nidentical, so start cannot safely create a keyed record.\n\nThe stop payload contains:\n\n- the parent UUID as `sessionId`;\n- the parent `events.jsonl` as `transcriptPath`;\n- the child UUID as `agentId`; and\n- `agentType` and `agentName`.\n\nBefore the stop hook runs, the parent transcript contains a `subagent.started`\nevent with the same top-level child UUID and the parent task `toolCallId`.\nChild tool events carry the same top-level child UUID and a\n`parentToolCallId` equal to that task ID. This is a deterministic join for\nconcurrent children and does not depend on descriptions, timestamps, ordering,\nor response text.\n\nCopilot stores all child events in the parent transcript; no standalone child\ntranscript exists. `subagent.completed` is appended only after the synchronous\nstop hook returns. Full per-child token breakdown appears later in\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics`, after the synchronous `sessionEnd` hook\nreturns. The adapter therefore cannot honestly attach the child transcript or\nexact token breakdown while handling the child completion.\n\n## Design\n\n### Hooks and upgrades\n\nEntire installs all nine Copilot hook commands, including `subagentStart` and\n`subagentStop`. `subagentStart` is parsed as an observed pass-through signal\nbecause it lacks a stable child identity. `subagentStop` drives durable capture.\n\nCopilot implements hook freshness reporting. A repository with any Entire-owned\nCopilot hook but without the full current command set is outdated, so an older\neight-hook installation is surfaced and a reinstall adds exactly the missing\nstart hook while preserving user hooks and unknown fields.\n\n### Stop correlation\n\nOn `subagentStop`, the adapter:\n\n1. opens Copilot's session store through `agent.SessionStore`;\n2. verifies that `transcriptPath` is exactly the expected\n   `<parent-session>/events.jsonl` beneath that store;\n3. reads it with the rooted no-follow API;\n4. finds the unique `subagent.started` whose top-level `agentId` matches the\n   stop payload; and\n5. uses its `data.toolCallId` as Entire's `ToolUseID`.\n\nZero or multiple identities produce no normalized event. The adapter does not\nfall back to parsing task result text.\n\nThe child file list is the deduplicated `filePaths` from\n`tool.execution_complete` events whose top-level child UUID matches and whose\n`parentToolCallId` equals the correlated task ID. Both the older\n`toolTelemetry.properties` and current `restrictedProperties` locations are\naccepted.\n\n### Shared lifecycle\n\nThe normalized stop is a true final `SubagentEnd` marked as a correlated\ncompletion learned without a launch marker. Shared lifecycle may create its\ntask record only if the parent session state already exists and is active.\nMissing or ended parent state is a no-op; no session can be resurrected.\n\nCompletion uses only adapter-supplied child files. It skips the whole-worktree\ndiff and child-transcript analyzer, both of which would over-attribute parent or\nconcurrent-child activity. The normal exactly-once task-record mutation handles\nduplicate stops and preserves one record per `ToolUseID`.\n\nEach record persists `transcript_unavailable: true`. Condensation still writes\n`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` but never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` fallback. This prevents an unrelated coincidental file from\nbeing attached to the Copilot child.\n\n### Tokens and transcript\n\nThe task record truthfully reports transcript unavailability and leaves child\ntoken usage unset. `subagent.completed.totalTokens` is exact but cannot be read\nuntil the stop hook returns, and the current `TokenUsage` schema has no\ntotal-only field. Mapping that total to input or output would be incorrect.\n\nParent-session transcript and token handling remains unchanged. A future\nCopilot hook exposing completed usage, or a future shared total-only token\nfield, can enrich the same task record without changing correlation.\n\n## Security and privacy\n\n- Hook-provided paths are never read with unrestricted `os.ReadFile`.\n- Parent transcript reads are confined to Copilot's session store and reject\n  outside paths, wrong layouts, and symlinks.\n- Unsafe session, task, and child IDs remain covered by central lifecycle\n  validation.\n- Logs contain operational IDs and errors, never prompts, responses, or file\n  contents.\n- Evidence fixtures committed to tests contain synthetic structure only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A fresh install has one managed start and stop hook; an old install is marked\n  outdated and upgrades idempotently.\n- Custom and `general-purpose` stops resolve to stable non-empty task IDs.\n- Two concurrent same-type children retain disjoint file lists.\n- A read-only child still creates a completed task record.\n- Duplicate, unmatched, missing-parent, and ended-parent stops create no extra\n  record and never resurrect state.\n- Condensation writes task metadata and never fabricates a child transcript.\n- Existing Copilot parent-session behavior and other agents remain unchanged.\n- Focused unit tests, the shared canary, repository checks, and an explicitly\n  authorized real Copilot end-user smoke test pass before push.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> Evidence-backed revision after real Copilot CLI 1.0.82 capture. Keep the\n> implementation near 450–700 additions and reuse shared task persistence.\n\n## 1. Capture the native contract\n\n- [x] Verify the official current Copilot release and isolate its home/cache.\n- [x] Run two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one\n  read-only.\n- [x] Run the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n- [x] Record structural hook/transcript fields only.\n- [x] Prove the child UUID → parent task ID join through the top-level\n  `agentId` on `subagent.started`.\n- [x] Prove file scoping through child `agentId` plus `parentToolCallId`.\n- [x] Confirm no standalone child transcript and that exact breakdown arrives\n  only after synchronous hooks finish.\n\n## 2. Install and detect the complete hook set\n\n- [x] Add `subagent-start` to `HookNames`, config mapping, and typed config.\n- [x] Cover fresh install, idempotency, force reinstall, and uninstall through\n  the existing loop-based tests.\n- [x] Add freshness detection so an old install missing only the start hook is\n  outdated and upgrades by one hook.\n\n## 3. Correlate stop payloads safely\n\n- [x] Extend the compatibility envelope with captured child metadata.\n- [x] Read the parent transcript through `SessionStore` with exact layout and\n  no-follow enforcement.\n- [x] Extract the unique task ID from `subagent.started` by child UUID.\n- [x] Extract only child-scoped file telemetry, supporting both `properties`\n  and `restrictedProperties`.\n- [x] Treat uncorrelatable start as pass-through and uncorrelatable stop as a\n  no-op.\n- [x] Test concurrent same-type children, general-purpose shape, ambiguity,\n  outside-store paths, and symlink rejection.\n\n## 4. Reuse durable task lifecycle\n\n- [x] Add a narrow normalized marker for completion learned without a launch\n  record.\n- [x] Permit record creation only inside an existing active parent session.\n- [x] Reuse `CompleteTaskRecord` for exactly-once completion.\n- [x] Use adapter-supplied files only; skip worktree and transcript scans.\n- [x] Persist transcript unavailability and make condensation skip generic\n  child-layout fallback.\n- [x] Test completion, duplicate stop, missing parent, and no-fallback\n  materialization.\n\n## 5. Strengthen shared end-to-end coverage\n\n- [x] Seed and commit a Copilot custom-agent fixture before Entire capture.\n- [x] Make the shared subagent E2E prompt explicitly delegate to that agent.\n- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run the paid real Copilot E2E.\n\n## 6. Documentation and verification\n\n- [x] Update the Copilot integration notes with the verified 1.0.82 contract.\n- [x] Update the agent-guide event matrix.\n- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` and remove accidental duplication.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check` before any commit.\n- [ ] Confirm final diff size remains below the redesign threshold.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run a wrapper-free real end-user smoke\n  using the candidate Entire binary and inspect the committed task record.\n- [ ] Commit only after local gates pass; push only when authorized, then wait\n  for all remote gates. Never merge without explicit approval.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"for the implementation.\n\n## Presence Detection\n\n- No repo-level `.copilot/` directory (unlike other agents)\n- `DetectPresence` delegates to `AreHooksInstalled`, which reads `.github/hooks/entire.json` and checks if any hook entry has an Entire command prefix (`entire ` or `go run \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"/cmd/entire/main.go `)\n- Simply having a `.github/hooks/` directory is NOT sufficient -- the directory must contain `entire.json` with Entire hook entries\n- Alternative: check for `copilot` binary in PATH\n\n## Protected Directories\n\n- `.github/hooks` — the hook config directory; listed in `ProtectedDirs()`, so Entire filters it out of change tracking and checkpoints\n- No agent-specific repo directory to protect\n\n## Subagent Lifecycle\n\nCopilot CLI 1.0.82 emits both native hooks for custom agents and the built-in\n`general-purpose` agent. `subagentStart` names the parent session and agent type but\ndoes not expose a child ID or task call ID; two concurrent same-type starts can be\nidentical, so Entire deliberately treats it as pass-through.\n\nAt true completion, `subagentStop` adds the child UUID as `agentId`. Before invoking\nthat hook, Copilot has already written `subagent.started` to the parent\n`events.jsonl`; that event carries the same top-level child UUID and the stable parent\ntask `toolCallId`. Entire reads the parent transcript through `SessionStore` and joins\non the UUID. Child tool events carry the same UUID plus `parentToolCallId`, allowing\ntwo concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\n\nCopilot does not create standalone child transcript files. Task metadata therefore\nrecords transcript unavailability and never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` layout. Per-child token breakdown is also unavailable at hook time:\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is authoritative but is appended only after\n`sessionEnd` returns. Entire leaves child token usage unset rather than misclassifying\nCopilot's total-only completion value.\n\n## Gaps & Limitations\n\n- No `Compaction` event — Copilot CLI doesn't appear to have a context compaction hook\n- No standalone child transcript; Copilot interleaves child events into the parent JSONL\n- Exact per-child token breakdown becomes available only after the last synchronous hook\n- `subagentStart` cannot be correlated safely and is retained as an observed pass-through hook\n- `transcriptPath` only available in `agentStop` hook — `userPromptSubmitted` and `sessionStart` don't include it, so we compute it from `~/.copilot/session-state/<sessionId>/events.jsonl`\n\n## Captured Payloads\n\n- Contract reverified on 2026-09-03 with Copilot CLI 1.0.82 using two\n  concurrent same-type custom agents (one writing, one read-only) and one\n  built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- Tests retain only synthetic structural fixtures; prompts, responses, and\n  local capture paths are not committed.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\n\n## Goal\n\nGive GitHub Copilot CLI durable, per-child task tracking using the shared Entire\nsubagent record and checkpoint format. Concurrent children must remain distinct,\nread-only children must still produce records, and ambiguous evidence must fail\nclosed rather than merge children together.\n\n## Verified Copilot contract\n\nThe contract was captured from the official Copilot CLI 1.0.82 release in an\nisolated repository. Three paid evidence invocations covered:\n\n- two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one read-only; and\n- the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n\nBoth custom and built-in children emit `subagentStart` and `subagentStop`.\nThe start payload contains the parent session ID, parent transcript path, and\nagent name, but no child UUID or task call ID. Two concurrent starts can be\nidentical, so start cannot safely create a keyed record.\n\nThe stop payload contains:\n\n- the parent UUID as `sessionId`;\n- the parent `events.jsonl` as `transcriptPath`;\n- the child UUID as `agentId`; and\n- `agentType` and `agentName`.\n\nBefore the stop hook runs, the parent transcript contains a `subagent.started`\nevent with the same top-level child UUID and the parent task `toolCallId`.\nChild tool events carry the same top-level child UUID and a\n`parentToolCallId` equal to that task ID. This is a deterministic join for\nconcurrent children and does not depend on descriptions, timestamps, ordering,\nor response text.\n\nCopilot stores all child events in the parent transcript; no standalone child\ntranscript exists. `subagent.completed` is appended only after the synchronous\nstop hook returns. Full per-child token breakdown appears later in\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics`, after the synchronous `sessionEnd` hook\nreturns. The adapter therefore cannot honestly attach the child transcript or\nexact token breakdown while handling the child completion.\n\n## Design\n\n### Hooks and upgrades\n\nEntire installs all nine Copilot hook commands, including `subagentStart` and\n`subagentStop`. `subagentStart` is parsed as an observed pass-through signal\nbecause it lacks a stable child identity. `subagentStop` drives durable capture.\n\nCopilot implements hook freshness reporting. A repository with any Entire-owned\nCopilot hook but without the full current command set is outdated, so an older\neight-hook installation is surfaced and a reinstall adds exactly the missing\nstart hook while preserving user hooks and unknown fields.\n\n### Stop correlation\n\nOn `subagentStop`, the adapter:\n\n1. opens Copilot's session store through `agent.SessionStore`;\n2. verifies that `transcriptPath` is exactly the expected\n   `<parent-session>/events.jsonl` beneath that store;\n3. reads it with the rooted no-follow API;\n4. finds the unique `subagent.started` whose top-level `agentId` matches the\n   stop payload; and\n5. uses its `data.toolCallId` as Entire's `ToolUseID`.\n\nZero or multiple identities produce no normalized event. The adapter does not\nfall back to parsing task result text.\n\nThe child file list is the deduplicated `filePaths` from\n`tool.execution_complete` events whose top-level child UUID matches and whose\n`parentToolCallId` equals the correlated task ID. Both the older\n`toolTelemetry.properties` and current `restrictedProperties` locations are\naccepted.\n\n### Shared lifecycle\n\nThe normalized stop is a true final `SubagentEnd` marked as a correlated\ncompletion learned without a launch marker. Shared lifecycle may create its\ntask record only if the parent session state already exists and is active.\nMissing or ended parent state is a no-op; no session can be resurrected.\n\nCompletion uses only adapter-supplied child files. It skips the whole-worktree\ndiff and child-transcript analyzer, both of which would over-attribute parent or\nconcurrent-child activity. The normal exactly-once task-record mutation handles\nduplicate stops and preserves one record per `ToolUseID`.\n\nEach record persists `transcript_unavailable: true`. Condensation still writes\n`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` but never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` fallback. This prevents an unrelated coincidental file from\nbeing attached to the Copilot child.\n\n### Tokens and transcript\n\nThe task record truthfully reports transcript unavailability and leaves child\ntoken usage unset. `subagent.completed.totalTokens` is exact but cannot be read\nuntil the stop hook returns, and the current `TokenUsage` schema has no\ntotal-only field. Mapping that total to input or output would be incorrect.\n\nParent-session transcript and token handling remains unchanged. A future\nCopilot hook exposing completed usage, or a future shared total-only token\nfield, can enrich the same task record without changing correlation.\n\n## Security and privacy\n\n- Hook-provided paths are never read with unrestricted `os.ReadFile`.\n- Parent transcript reads are confined to Copilot's session store and reject\n  outside paths, wrong layouts, and symlinks.\n- Unsafe session, task, and child IDs remain covered by central lifecycle\n  validation.\n- Logs contain operational IDs and errors, never prompts, responses, or file\n  contents.\n- Evidence fixtures committed to tests contain synthetic structure only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A fresh install has one managed start and stop hook; an old install is marked\n  outdated and upgrades idempotently.\n- Custom and `general-purpose` stops resolve to stable non-empty task IDs.\n- Two concurrent same-type children retain disjoint file lists.\n- A read-only child still creates a completed task record.\n- Duplicate, unmatched, missing-parent, and ended-parent stops create no extra\n  record and never resurrect state.\n- Condensation writes task metadata and never fabricates a child transcript.\n- Existing Copilot parent-session behavior and other agents remain unchanged.\n- Focused unit tests, the shared canary, repository checks, and an explicitly\n  authorized real Copilot end-user smoke test pass before push.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> Evidence-backed revision after real Copilot CLI 1.0.82 capture. Keep the\n> implementation near 450–700 additions and reuse shared task persistence.\n\n## 1. Capture the native contract\n\n- [x] Verify the official current Copilot release and isolate its home/cache.\n- [x] Run two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one\n  read-only.\n- [x] Run the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n- [x] Record structural hook/transcript fields only.\n- [x] Prove the child UUID → parent task ID join through the top-level\n  `agentId` on `subagent.started`.\n- [x] Prove file scoping through child `agentId` plus `parentToolCallId`.\n- [x] Confirm no standalone child transcript and that exact breakdown arrives\n  only after synchronous hooks finish.\n\n## 2. Install and detect the complete hook set\n\n- [x] Add `subagent-start` to `HookNames`, config mapping, and typed config.\n- [x] Cover fresh install, idempotency, force reinstall, and uninstall through\n  the existing loop-based tests.\n- [x] Add freshness detection so an old install missing only the start hook is\n  outdated and upgrades by one hook.\n\n## 3. Correlate stop payloads safely\n\n- [x] Extend the compatibility envelope with captured child metadata.\n- [x] Read the parent transcript through `SessionStore` with exact layout and\n  no-follow enforcement.\n- [x] Extract the unique task ID from `subagent.started` by child UUID.\n- [x] Extract only child-scoped file telemetry, supporting both `properties`\n  and `restrictedProperties`.\n- [x] Treat uncorrelatable start as pass-through and uncorrelatable stop as a\n  no-op.\n- [x] Test concurrent same-type children, general-purpose shape, ambiguity,\n  outside-store paths, and symlink rejection.\n\n## 4. Reuse durable task lifecycle\n\n- [x] Add a narrow normalized marker for completion learned without a launch\n  record.\n- [x] Permit record creation only inside an existing active parent session.\n- [x] Reuse `CompleteTaskRecord` for exactly-once completion.\n- [x] Use adapter-supplied files only; skip worktree and transcript scans.\n- [x] Persist transcript unavailability and make condensation skip generic\n  child-layout fallback.\n- [x] Test completion, duplicate stop, missing parent, and no-fallback\n  materialization.\n\n## 5. Strengthen shared end-to-end coverage\n\n- [x] Seed and commit a Copilot custom-agent fixture before Entire capture.\n- [x] Make the shared subagent E2E prompt explicitly delegate to that agent.\n- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run the paid real Copilot E2E.\n\n## 6. Documentation and verification\n\n- [x] Update the Copilot integration notes with the verified 1.0.82 contract.\n- [x] Update the agent-guide event matrix.\n- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` and remove accidental duplication.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check` before any commit.\n- [ ] Confirm final diff size remains below the redesign threshold.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run a wrapper-free real end-user smoke\n  using the candidate Entire binary and inspect the committed task record.\n- [ ] Commit only after local gates pass; push only when authorized, then wait\n  for all remote gates. Never merge without explicit approval.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3000},"formatted_output":"for the implementation.\n\n## Presence Detection\n\n- No repo-level `.copilot/` directory (unlike other agents)\n- `DetectPresence` delegates to `AreHooksInstalled`, which reads `.github/hooks/entire.json` and checks if any hook entry has an Entire command prefix (`entire ` or `go run \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"/cmd/entire/main.go `)\n- Simply having a `.github/hooks/` directory is NOT sufficient -- the directory must contain `entire.json` with Entire hook entries\n- Alternative: check for `copilot` binary in PATH\n\n## Protected Directories\n\n- `.github/hooks` — the hook config directory; listed in `ProtectedDirs()`, so Entire filters it out of change tracking and checkpoints\n- No agent-specific repo directory to protect\n\n## Subagent Lifecycle\n\nCopilot CLI 1.0.82 emits both native hooks for custom agents and the built-in\n`general-purpose` agent. `subagentStart` names the parent session and agent type but\ndoes not expose a child ID or task call ID; two concurrent same-type starts can be\nidentical, so Entire deliberately treats it as pass-through.\n\nAt true completion, `subagentStop` adds the child UUID as `agentId`. Before invoking\nthat hook, Copilot has already written `subagent.started` to the parent\n`events.jsonl`; that event carries the same top-level child UUID and the stable parent\ntask `toolCallId`. Entire reads the parent transcript through `SessionStore` and joins\non the UUID. Child tool events carry the same UUID plus `parentToolCallId`, allowing\ntwo concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\n\nCopilot does not create standalone child transcript files. Task metadata therefore\nrecords transcript unavailability and never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` layout. Per-child token breakdown is also unavailable at hook time:\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics` is authoritative but is appended only after\n`sessionEnd` returns. Entire leaves child token usage unset rather than misclassifying\nCopilot's total-only completion value.\n\n## Gaps & Limitations\n\n- No `Compaction` event — Copilot CLI doesn't appear to have a context compaction hook\n- No standalone child transcript; Copilot interleaves child events into the parent JSONL\n- Exact per-child token breakdown becomes available only after the last synchronous hook\n- `subagentStart` cannot be correlated safely and is retained as an observed pass-through hook\n- `transcriptPath` only available in `agentStop` hook — `userPromptSubmitted` and `sessionStart` don't include it, so we compute it from `~/.copilot/session-state/<sessionId>/events.jsonl`\n\n## Captured Payloads\n\n- Contract reverified on 2026-09-03 with Copilot CLI 1.0.82 using two\n  concurrent same-type custom agents (one writing, one read-only) and one\n  built-in `general-purpose` agent.\n- Tests retain only synthetic structural fixtures; prompts, responses, and\n  local capture paths are not committed.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Design\n\n## Goal\n\nGive GitHub Copilot CLI durable, per-child task tracking using the shared Entire\nsubagent record and checkpoint format. Concurrent children must remain distinct,\nread-only children must still produce records, and ambiguous evidence must fail\nclosed rather than merge children together.\n\n## Verified Copilot contract\n\nThe contract was captured from the official Copilot CLI 1.0.82 release in an\nisolated repository. Three paid evidence invocations covered:\n\n- two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one read-only; and\n- the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n\nBoth custom and built-in children emit `subagentStart` and `subagentStop`.\nThe start payload contains the parent session ID, parent transcript path, and\nagent name, but no child UUID or task call ID. Two concurrent starts can be\nidentical, so start cannot safely create a keyed record.\n\nThe stop payload contains:\n\n- the parent UUID as `sessionId`;\n- the parent `events.jsonl` as `transcriptPath`;\n- the child UUID as `agentId`; and\n- `agentType` and `agentName`.\n\nBefore the stop hook runs, the parent transcript contains a `subagent.started`\nevent with the same top-level child UUID and the parent task `toolCallId`.\nChild tool events carry the same top-level child UUID and a\n`parentToolCallId` equal to that task ID. This is a deterministic join for\nconcurrent children and does not depend on descriptions, timestamps, ordering,\nor response text.\n\nCopilot stores all child events in the parent transcript; no standalone child\ntranscript exists. `subagent.completed` is appended only after the synchronous\nstop hook returns. Full per-child token breakdown appears later in\n`session.shutdown.agentMetrics`, after the synchronous `sessionEnd` hook\nreturns. The adapter therefore cannot honestly attach the child transcript or\nexact token breakdown while handling the child completion.\n\n## Design\n\n### Hooks and upgrades\n\nEntire installs all nine Copilot hook commands, including `subagentStart` and\n`subagentStop`. `subagentStart` is parsed as an observed pass-through signal\nbecause it lacks a stable child identity. `subagentStop` drives durable capture.\n\nCopilot implements hook freshness reporting. A repository with any Entire-owned\nCopilot hook but without the full current command set is outdated, so an older\neight-hook installation is surfaced and a reinstall adds exactly the missing\nstart hook while preserving user hooks and unknown fields.\n\n### Stop correlation\n\nOn `subagentStop`, the adapter:\n\n1. opens Copilot's session store through `agent.SessionStore`;\n2. verifies that `transcriptPath` is exactly the expected\n   `<parent-session>/events.jsonl` beneath that store;\n3. reads it with the rooted no-follow API;\n4. finds the unique `subagent.started` whose top-level `agentId` matches the\n   stop payload; and\n5. uses its `data.toolCallId` as Entire's `ToolUseID`.\n\nZero or multiple identities produce no normalized event. The adapter does not\nfall back to parsing task result text.\n\nThe child file list is the deduplicated `filePaths` from\n`tool.execution_complete` events whose top-level child UUID matches and whose\n`parentToolCallId` equals the correlated task ID. Both the older\n`toolTelemetry.properties` and current `restrictedProperties` locations are\naccepted.\n\n### Shared lifecycle\n\nThe normalized stop is a true final `SubagentEnd` marked as a correlated\ncompletion learned without a launch marker. Shared lifecycle may create its\ntask record only if the parent session state already exists and is active.\nMissing or ended parent state is a no-op; no session can be resurrected.\n\nCompletion uses only adapter-supplied child files. It skips the whole-worktree\ndiff and child-transcript analyzer, both of which would over-attribute parent or\nconcurrent-child activity. The normal exactly-once task-record mutation handles\nduplicate stops and preserves one record per `ToolUseID`.\n\nEach record persists `transcript_unavailable: true`. Condensation still writes\n`tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json` but never probes the generic Claude-style\n`agent-<id>.jsonl` fallback. This prevents an unrelated coincidental file from\nbeing attached to the Copilot child.\n\n### Tokens and transcript\n\nThe task record truthfully reports transcript unavailability and leaves child\ntoken usage unset. `subagent.completed.totalTokens` is exact but cannot be read\nuntil the stop hook returns, and the current `TokenUsage` schema has no\ntotal-only field. Mapping that total to input or output would be incorrect.\n\nParent-session transcript and token handling remains unchanged. A future\nCopilot hook exposing completed usage, or a future shared total-only token\nfield, can enrich the same task record without changing correlation.\n\n## Security and privacy\n\n- Hook-provided paths are never read with unrestricted `os.ReadFile`.\n- Parent transcript reads are confined to Copilot's session store and reject\n  outside paths, wrong layouts, and symlinks.\n- Unsafe session, task, and child IDs remain covered by central lifecycle\n  validation.\n- Logs contain operational IDs and errors, never prompts, responses, or file\n  contents.\n- Evidence fixtures committed to tests contain synthetic structure only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A fresh install has one managed start and stop hook; an old install is marked\n  outdated and upgrades idempotently.\n- Custom and `general-purpose` stops resolve to stable non-empty task IDs.\n- Two concurrent same-type children retain disjoint file lists.\n- A read-only child still creates a completed task record.\n- Duplicate, unmatched, missing-parent, and ended-parent stops create no extra\n  record and never resurrect state.\n- Condensation writes task metadata and never fabricates a child transcript.\n- Existing Copilot parent-session behavior and other agents remain unchanged.\n- Focused unit tests, the shared canary, repository checks, and an explicitly\n  authorized real Copilot end-user smoke test pass before push.\n# Copilot CLI Native Subagent Tracking Implementation Plan\n\n> Evidence-backed revision after real Copilot CLI 1.0.82 capture. Keep the\n> implementation near 450–700 additions and reuse shared task persistence.\n\n## 1. Capture the native contract\n\n- [x] Verify the official current Copilot release and isolate its home/cache.\n- [x] Run two concurrent same-type custom children, one writing and one\n  read-only.\n- [x] Run the built-in `general-purpose` child.\n- [x] Record structural hook/transcript fields only.\n- [x] Prove the child UUID → parent task ID join through the top-level\n  `agentId` on `subagent.started`.\n- [x] Prove file scoping through child `agentId` plus `parentToolCallId`.\n- [x] Confirm no standalone child transcript and that exact breakdown arrives\n  only after synchronous hooks finish.\n\n## 2. Install and detect the complete hook set\n\n- [x] Add `subagent-start` to `HookNames`, config mapping, and typed config.\n- [x] Cover fresh install, idempotency, force reinstall, and uninstall through\n  the existing loop-based tests.\n- [x] Add freshness detection so an old install missing only the start hook is\n  outdated and upgrades by one hook.\n\n## 3. Correlate stop payloads safely\n\n- [x] Extend the compatibility envelope with captured child metadata.\n- [x] Read the parent transcript through `SessionStore` with exact layout and\n  no-follow enforcement.\n- [x] Extract the unique task ID from `subagent.started` by child UUID.\n- [x] Extract only child-scoped file telemetry, supporting both `properties`\n  and `restrictedProperties`.\n- [x] Treat uncorrelatable start as pass-through and uncorrelatable stop as a\n  no-op.\n- [x] Test concurrent same-type children, general-purpose shape, ambiguity,\n  outside-store paths, and symlink rejection.\n\n## 4. Reuse durable task lifecycle\n\n- [x] Add a narrow normalized marker for completion learned without a launch\n  record.\n- [x] Permit record creation only inside an existing active parent session.\n- [x] Reuse `CompleteTaskRecord` for exactly-once completion.\n- [x] Use adapter-supplied files only; skip worktree and transcript scans.\n- [x] Persist transcript unavailability and make condensation skip generic\n  child-layout fallback.\n- [x] Test completion, duplicate stop, missing parent, and no-fallback\n  materialization.\n\n## 5. Strengthen shared end-to-end coverage\n\n- [x] Seed and commit a Copilot custom-agent fixture before Entire capture.\n- [x] Make the shared subagent E2E prompt explicitly delegate to that agent.\n- [ ] Run the deterministic Vogon canary.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run the paid real Copilot E2E.\n\n## 6. Documentation and verification\n\n- [x] Update the Copilot integration notes with the verified 1.0.82 contract.\n- [x] Update the agent-guide event matrix.\n- [ ] Run focused package tests and broader affected-package tests.\n- [ ] Run `mise run dup` and remove accidental duplication.\n- [ ] Run `mise run check` before any commit.\n- [ ] Confirm final diff size remains below the redesign threshold.\n- [ ] With separate user authorization, run a wrapper-free real end-user smoke\n  using the candidate Entire binary and inspect the committed task record.\n- [ ] Commit only after local gates pass; push only when authorized, then wait\n  for all remote gates. Never merge without explicit approval.\n"},"started_at_ms":1788541773305,"completed_at_ms":1788541773305}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:09:33.308Z","ordinal":11625,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a06aeb-fba1-7c73-b9bd-e6c66f69b450","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-604da87d-a900-42cb-8bcc-8dc446cc85fb","process_id":"90859","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,220p' mise.toml"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' mise.toml","name":"mise.toml","path":"mise.toml"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"[tools]\n# Please also keep the version aligned in the go.mod file\ngo = { version = '1.26.6', postinstall = \"go install github.com/go-delve/delve/cmd/dlv@latest && go install gotest.tools/gotestsum@latest\" }\ngolangci-lint = '2.11.3'\nshellcheck = 'latest'\ntmux = 'latest'\n\"go:github.com/entireio/roger-roger/cmd/roger-roger\" = 'latest'\n\"go:github.com/entireio/roger-roger/cmd/entire-agent-roger-roger\" = 'latest'\n\n[tasks.fmt]\ndescription = \"Run gofmt\"\nrun = \"gofmt -s -w .\"\n\n[tasks.test]\ndescription = \"Run tests\"\nrun = \"gotestsum --format pkgname --format-icons text --format-hide-empty-pkg --hide-summary skipped -- ./...\"\n\n[tasks.\"test:integration\"]\ndescription = \"Run integration tests\"\nrun = \"gotestsum --format testname --format-icons text --hide-summary skipped -- -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/... ./cmd/entire/cli/auth/...\"\n\n[tasks.\"test:ci\"]\ndescription = \"Run all tests (unit + integration + E2E canary) with race detection\"\nrun = \"\"\"\ngo test -tags=integration -race ./...\nmise run test:e2e:canary\n\"\"\"\n\n[tasks.check]\ndescription = \"Run formatting, linting, and CI tests\"\ndepends = [\"fmt\", \"lint\", \"test:ci\"]\n\n[tasks.\"build:windows\"]\ndescription = \"Cross-compile for Windows amd64\"\nrun = \"CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=window