{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:34:31.708Z","ordinal":12175,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a081dc-6d8d-77f3-bc0a-5b28bab962d1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa03914ccfc87d091d2fd8e450a6cd0","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The artifact inspection caught an important false positive: the end-to-end checkpoint contains `docs/red.md`, but it contains no `tasks/<tool-use-id>/task.json`. In 1.0.63, the parent turn still attributed the file, allowing the existing assertion to pass even though the subagent record was not materialized.\n\nSo the paid test did not yet validate the feature strongly enough. I’m tracing the sanitized 1.0.63 transcript shape now, then I’ll fix either the compatibility parser or the E2E assertion—and rerun the same paid test—without adding broad new test surface."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788885268837,"completed_at_ms":1788885271708}}
