{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:38:10.013Z","ordinal":12268,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a081dc-6d8d-77f3-bc0a-5b28bab962d1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa039eeb94087d0873773677cef4197","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The strengthened assertion correctly found a task record for Vogon, but it also exposed that `roger-roger` is a generic external-agent fake that does not model subagent task records. That is outside this Copilot-specific contract, so applying the new assertion universally would break an unrelated canary.\n\nI’m scoping the task-record assertion to Copilot CLI only. The shared file/checkpoint assertions remain universal; Copilot’s extra assertion is the one specifically needed to prevent today’s false positive."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788885487251,"completed_at_ms":1788885490013}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:38:10.015Z","ordinal":12269,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa039eeb94087d0873773677cef4197","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The strengthened assertion correctly found a task record for Vogon, but it also exposed that `roger-roger` is a generic external-agent fake that does not model subagent task records. That is outside this Copilot-specific contract, so applying the new assertion universally would break an unrelated canary.\n\nI’m scoping the task-record assertion to Copilot CLI only. The shared file/checkpoint assertions remain universal; Copilot’s extra assertion is the one specifically needed to prevent today’s false positive."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a081dc-6d8d-77f3-bc0a-5b28bab962d1","create_time":1788885478.319609,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:38:15.446Z","ordinal":12270,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa039f1cd7487d085081c2945917753","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9BRWjkVJ4eJuuFtiPFOjgzwW","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go\\n@@\\n \\t\\tcpID := testutil.AssertHasCheckpointTrailer(t, s.Dir, \\\"HEAD\\\")\\n \\t\\ttestutil.AssertCheckpointExists(t, s.Dir, cpID)\\n-\\t\\ttestutil.AssertCheckpointHasTaskRecord(t, s.Dir, cpID)\\n+\\t\\tif s.Agent.Name() == \\\"copilot-cli\\\" {\\n+\\t\\t\\ttestutil.AssertCheckpointHasTaskRecord(t, s.Dir, cpID)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\\n@@\\n At true completion, `subagentStop` adds the child UUID as `agentId`. Before invoking\\n that hook, Copilot has already written `subagent.started` to the parent\\n `events.jsonl`; that event carries the same top-level child UUID and the stable parent\\n task `toolCallId`. Entire reads the parent transcript through `SessionStore` and joins\\n on the UUID. Child tool events carry the same UUID plus `parentToolCallId`, allowing\\n two concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\\n+Copilot 1.0.63 omits the stop `agentId`; Entire falls back only when exactly one\\n+not-yet-completed start matches the stop's agent name, so ambiguous concurrent\\n+children still fail closed.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a081dc-6d8d-77f3-bc0a-5b28bab962d1","create_time":1788885478.319609}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:38:15.609Z","ordinal":12271,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a081dc-6d8d-77f3-bc0a-5b28bab962d1","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-8a4ee227-5df4-4b61-bb94-518c15755ba4","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -216,2 +216,5 @@\n two concurrent children to receive disjoint file lists even when they share a type.\n+Copilot 1.0.63 omits the stop `agentId`; Entire falls back only when exactly one\n+not-yet-completed start matches the stop's agent name, so ambiguous concurrent\n+children still fail closed.\n \n","move_path":null},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -36,3 +36,5 @@\n \t\ttestutil.AssertCheckpointExists(t, s.Dir, cpID)\n-\t\ttestutil.AssertCheckpointHasTaskRecord(t, s.Dir, cpID)\n+\t\tif s.Agent.Name() == \"copilot-cli\" {\n+\t\t\ttestutil.AssertCheckpointHasTaskRecord(t, s.Dir, cpID)\n+\t\t}\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/e2e/tests/subagent_commit_flow_test.go\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/AGENT.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788885495492,"completed_at_ms":1788885495609}}
