{"timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:42:30.952Z","ordinal":12340,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a081dc-6d8d-77f3-bc0a-5b28bab962d1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa03af115c487d083b970047606b2dd","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The paid Copilot E2E now genuinely passes.\n\nThe first run exposed a false positive: the checkpoint had `docs/red.md` but no task record. Copilot 1.0.63 omits `agentId` from `subagentStop`, so I added a safe fallback that accepts exactly one incomplete matching agent name and fails closed on ambiguity.\n\nAfter strengthening the E2E assertion:\n\n- Real Copilot CLI 1.0.63: 1/1 passed.\n- Durable task created at `tasks/toolu_…/task.json` ([artifact evidence](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/e2e/artifacts/2026-09-08T09-39-34/TestSubagentCommitFlow-copilot-cli/git-tree.txt:15>)).\n- Lifecycle recorded the correlated completion ([log](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents/e2e/artifacts/2026-09-08T09-39-34/TestSubagentCommitFlow-copilot-cli/entire-logs/entire.log:55>)).\n- Focused Vogon and roger-roger canaries passed.\n- Copilot package tests passed.\n- Lint: zero issues.\n\nThe diff is now 790 insertions, 190 deletions—600 net lines. Nothing is committed or pushed yet."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1788885745115,"completed_at_ms":1788885750952}}
