{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:14:11.603Z","ordinal":12504,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a086f2-c293-7681-a42b-8982f04f3fab","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"You are in 'explanatory' output style mode, where you should provide educational insights about the codebase as you help with the user's task.\n\nYou should be clear and educational, providing helpful explanations while remaining focused on the task. Balance educational content with task completion. When providing insights, you may exceed typical length constraints, but remain focused and relevant.\n\n## Insights\nIn order to encourage learning, before and after writing code, always provide brief educational explanations about implementation choices using (with backticks):\n\"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n[2-3 key educational points]\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\"\n\nThese insights should be included in the conversation, not in the codebase. You should generally focus on interesting insights that are specific to the codebase or the code you just wrote, rather than general programming concepts. Do not wait until the end to provide insights. Provide them as you write code."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","create_time":1788970451.6037,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:14:20.309Z","ordinal":12505,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa185d8781487d09376e845151f4656","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes—I ran both:\n\n- The paid E2E test, which invokes `copilot -p` through the Go harness.\n- A separate wrapper-free `copilot -p` smoke test in an isolated repository, with no test harness and no retries.\n\nThe direct test passed on Copilot CLI 1.0.63:\n\n- Copilot launched the named `entire-direct-smoke` subagent.\n- The subagent created `docs/direct-smoke.md`.\n- Entire recorded one completed task with ID `REDACTED`.\n- A normal Git commit created checkpoint `01M23F3ZP35KVBTYGRX3RJ1AQG`.\n- The permanent checkpoint ref contains the subagent’s `task.json`.\n- Parent checkpoint metadata includes the modified file.\n- The shadow branch was cleaned up afterward.\n\nThe isolated smoke repository is:\n\n`/private/tmp/copilot-direct-smoke.XMTUsb`\n\nOne version-specific detail: Copilot 1.0.63 does not provide per-file telemetry in its subagent events, so the task record correctly marks its child transcript unavailable while the parent checkpoint records the changed file. Copilot 1.0.82’s newer event format supports exact child-file attribution.\n\nSo this is now validated as an actual end-user flow—not only an E2E simulation. The feature-branch changes themselves remain uncommitted and unpushed."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1788970456646,"completed_at_ms":1788970460309}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:14:20.315Z","ordinal":12506,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa185d8781487d09376e845151f4656","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Yes—I ran both:\n\n- The paid E2E test, which invokes `copilot -p` through the Go harness.\n- A separate wrapper-free `copilot -p` smoke test in an isolated repository, with no test harness and no retries.\n\nThe direct test passed on Copilot CLI 1.0.63:\n\n- Copilot launched the named `entire-direct-smoke` subagent.\n- The subagent created `docs/direct-smoke.md`.\n- Entire recorded one completed task with ID `REDACTED`.\n- A normal Git commit created checkpoint `01M23F3ZP35KVBTYGRX3RJ1AQG`.\n- The permanent checkpoint ref contains the subagent’s `task.json`.\n- Parent checkpoint metadata includes the modified file.\n- The shadow branch was cleaned up afterward.\n\nThe isolated smoke repository is:\n\n`/private/tmp/copilot-direct-smoke.XMTUsb`\n\nOne version-specific detail: Copilot 1.0.63 does not provide per-file telemetry in its subagent events, so the task record correctly marks its child transcript unavailable while the parent checkpoint records the changed file. Copilot 1.0.82’s newer event format supports exact child-file attribution.\n\nSo this is now validated as an actual end-user flow—not only an E2E simulation. The feature-branch changes themselves remain uncommitted and unpushed."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a082bc-1971-70f0-aecc-959aea46ada6","create_time":1788970455.677049,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
