{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:18:39.348Z","ordinal":12694,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08840-5c8f-75b0-ae2e-d14d37ea77c7","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1db3dbae087d0b488e8940c4ed636","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes—this is a legitimate test-harness bug, not something we should normalize as an exception. I’ll fix it narrowly so local replacement paths containing spaces are represented correctly, prove the test fails before and passes after, then rerun the affected package and required gates. I’m using the systematic-debugging and test-driven-development guidance for that sequence."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788992317778,"completed_at_ms":1788992319348}}
