{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:19:22.610Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1db63d3d087d0ad9ae657daa4e60c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08840-5c8f-75b0-ae2e-d14d37ea77c7"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:19:26.946Z","ordinal":12734,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08840-5c8f-75b0-ae2e-d14d37ea77c7","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1db6a8cb087d0b0a7b156bef27a1c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Yes. It is a real portability bug in the test.\n\nRoot cause: the test interpolates the repository path directly into `go.mod`. Go module syntax treats spaces as separators, so the generated `replace` directive is invalid in this checkout.\n\nThe narrow options are:\n\n1. Quote the replacement path with `strconv.Quote`—one import and one expression change.\n2. Generate the file through `golang.org/x/mod/modfile`—robust but unnecessarily larger.\n3. Run `go mod edit -replace`—adds another subprocess and error path.\n\nI recommend option 1. The existing failing test already provides the red TDD case in this space-containing checkout; after the one-line fix, I’ll run it directly and then rerun `mise run check` without exclusions. No new test or design-document bloat.\n\nThe original checkpoint could not be retrieved locally, so this diagnosis is inferred from the code and reproduced failure. Shall I apply that narrow fix?"}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1788992362661,"completed_at_ms":1788992366945}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:19:26.947Z","ordinal":12735,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1db6a8cb087d0b0a7b156bef27a1c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Yes. It is a real portability bug in the test.\n\nRoot cause: the test interpolates the repository path directly into `go.mod`. Go module syntax treats spaces as separators, so the generated `replace` directive is invalid in this checkout.\n\nThe narrow options are:\n\n1. Quote the replacement path with `strconv.Quote`—one import and one expression change.\n2. Generate the file through `golang.org/x/mod/modfile`—robust but unnecessarily larger.\n3. Run `go mod edit -replace`—adds another subprocess and error path.\n\nI recommend option 1. The existing failing test already provides the red TDD case in this space-containing checkout; after the one-line fix, I’ll run it directly and then rerun `mise run check` without exclusions. No new test or design-document bloat.\n\nThe original checkpoint could not be retrieved locally, so this diagnosis is inferred from the code and reproduced failure. Shall I apply that narrow fix?"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08840-5c8f-75b0-ae2e-d14d37ea77c7","create_time":1788992355.103037,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
