{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:22:50.594Z","ordinal":12759,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08843-ddc1-7f32-a410-1ad4096c77a1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1dc38002c87d0b96b6226eda154c5","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Not `strconv.Quote` specifically. The repository has no other test that generates a `go.mod` replacement path.\n\nThe closest codebase norm is `fmt.Sprintf(... %q ...)` when inserting dynamic values into generated configuration. The repo uses that pattern in several test fixtures, while `golang.org/x/mod/modfile` is currently used only for parsing.\n\nSo I’d revise the fix to:\n\n- Build the small `go.mod` fixture with `fmt.Sprintf`.\n- Insert `filepath.ToSlash(repoRoot)` using `%q`.\n- Add only the `fmt` import.\n- Keep the existing test as the regression coverage.\n\nThat is equally safe, more consistent with this codebase, and still only a tiny test-only change. If that sounds right, I’ll implement it."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1788992568056,"completed_at_ms":1788992570594}}
