{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:55:31.214Z","ordinal":13065,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1e3dd220c87d0af1912a8d6ecc432","status":"completed","call_id":"call_rIfbuGQcKoMyrFbdDzb9LJiv","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr create -R entireio/cli --base main --head feat/copilot-subagent-tracking --title 'feat(copilot-cli): track subagent tasks' --body '## Summary\\n\\n- handle Copilot CLI subagent lifecycle hooks and persist completed task records into checkpoints\\n- correlate modern agent IDs directly and support Copilot CLI 1.0.63 through a fail-closed unique unfinished-name fallback\\n- preserve task records through manual-commit condensation and verify them in the real-agent E2E flow\\n- quote the Betterleaks test fixture replacement path so the full suite works from checkout paths containing spaces\\n\\n## Compatibility and behavior\\n\\nCopilot CLI 1.0.82 exposes the child UUID and per-file tool telemetry, allowing exact child-file attribution. Copilot CLI 1.0.63 omits the ID from subagentStop, so Entire correlates only one unambiguous unfinished subagent.started event with the same agent name. Ambiguous matches fail closed. Copilot does not expose a child transcript path, so the task record records why that transcript is unavailable.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- mise run check\\n- paid real-agent E2E: TestSubagentCommitFlow with copilot-cli\\n- wrapper-free copilot -p smoke using a named subagent, followed by a normal Git commit; verified the checkpoint task record and shadow-branch cleanup\\n\\n## Rollout\\n\\nNo migration is required. Existing Copilot sessions without subagent events retain their current behavior.'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":12000,\"sandbox_permissions\":\"require_escalated\",\"justification\":\"Allow creating the Copilot subagent-tracking pull request in entireio/cli?\",\"prefix_rule\":[\"gh\",\"pr\",\"create\"]}); text(r.output); text(`exit_code=${r.exit_code}`);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08861-a963-7db3-b7f4-840a0a3e6fdf","create_time":1788994516.101039}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T22:55:37.555Z","ordinal":13066,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08861-a963-7db3-b7f4-840a0a3e6fdf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-92d70433-14d0-4c90-a305-9def967d195c","process_id":"95775","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr create -R entireio/cli --base main --head feat/copilot-subagent-tracking --title 'feat(copilot-cli): track subagent tasks' --body '## Summary\n\n- handle Copilot CLI subagent lifecycle hooks and persist completed task records into checkpoints\n- correlate modern agent IDs directly and support Copilot CLI 1.0.63 through a fail-closed unique unfinished-name fallback\n- preserve task records through manual-commit condensation and verify them in the real-agent E2E flow\n- quote the Betterleaks test fixture replacement path so the full suite works from checkout paths containing spaces\n\n## Compatibility and behavior\n\nCopilot CLI 1.0.82 exposes the child UUID and per-file tool telemetry, allowing exact child-file attribution. Copilot CLI 1.0.63 omits the ID from subagentStop, so Entire correlates only one unambiguous unfinished subagent.started event with the same agent name. Ambiguous matches fail closed. Copilot does not expose a child transcript path, so the task record records why that transcript is unavailable.\n\n## Validation\n\n- mise run check\n- paid real-agent E2E: TestSubagentCommitFlow with copilot-cli\n- wrapper-free copilot -p smoke using a named subagent, followed by a normal Git commit; verified the checkpoint task record and shadow-branch cleanup\n\n## Rollout\n\nNo migration is required. Existing Copilot sessions without subagent events retain their current behavior.'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr create -R entireio/cli --base main --head feat/copilot-subagent-tracking --title 'feat(copilot-cli): track subagent tasks' --body '## Summary\n\n- handle Copilot CLI subagent lifecycle hooks and persist completed task records into checkpoints\n- correlate modern agent IDs directly and support Copilot CLI 1.0.63 through a fail-closed unique unfinished-name fallback\n- preserve task records through manual-commit condensation and verify them in the real-agent E2E flow\n- quote the Betterleaks test fixture replacement path so the full suite works from checkout paths containing spaces\n\n## Compatibility and behavior\n\nCopilot CLI 1.0.82 exposes the child UUID and per-file tool telemetry, allowing exact child-file attribution. Copilot CLI 1.0.63 omits the ID from subagentStop, so Entire correlates only one unambiguous unfinished subagent.started event with the same agent name. Ambiguous matches fail closed. Copilot does not expose a child transcript path, so the task record records why that transcript is unavailable.\n\n## Validation\n\n- mise run check\n- paid real-agent E2E: TestSubagentCommitFlow with copilot-cli\n- wrapper-free copilot -p smoke using a named subagent, followed by a normal Git commit; verified the checkpoint task record and shadow-branch cleanup\n\n## Rollout\n\nNo migration is required. Existing Copilot sessions without subagent events retain their current behavior.'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2341\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2341\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":103536541},"formatted_output":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2341\n"},"started_at_ms":1788994535451,"completed_at_ms":1788994537555}}
