{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T23:13:11.839Z","ordinal":13425,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08861-a963-7db3-b7f4-840a0a3e6fdf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f08dbafc-aad3-4fbf-b200-899e90348388","process_id":"60800","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","entire api --to cell '/api/v1/trails/gh/entireio/cli/1282/reviews/comments'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire api --to cell '/api/v1/trails/gh/entireio/cli/1282/reviews/comments'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io/api/v1/schemas/ReviewCommentsListResponseBody.json\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"01M246JW5HX5Z39W4H1DPQ3AF0\",\n      \"trailId\": \"01M2464KM3DMQYQ7WVMHE637R0\",\n      \"repositoryId\": \"01KSFAN13YPQ0EWBV5KRE7F5HV\",\n      \"reviewId\": \"01M246JW549DF3JEP3VJ79XJPW\",\n      \"codeVersionId\": \"01M246JW4YTXCZ0CV7YP2YKGHD\",\n      \"actorId\": \"agent:trail-review\",\n      \"actorDisplayName\": null,\n      \"body\": \"When `record.TranscriptUnavailable` is true, this branch appends `payload` (built from `record.AgentID` at line 363) and `continue`s *before* the `record.AgentID == \\\"\\\" || validation.ValidateAgentID(record.AgentID) != nil` guard at line 400 runs. That guard exists specifically, per this function's own doc comment above, to stop an unsafe `AgentID` from reaching `writeTaskRecordEntries` in `checkpoint/persistent.go`, which unconditionally re-validates `task.AgentID` and returns a hard `fmt.Errorf` on failure. That error propagates out of `applySessionWrite` and fails the *entire* checkpoint write (not just this task), directly violating the stated invariant that \\\"a poisoned record produces zero payloads, not an error.\\\" The `TranscriptUnavailable` short-circuit should validate `record.AgentID` the same way before appending, or fall through to the existing check below.\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"statusReason\": null,\n      \"statusActorId\": null,\n      \"statusActorDisplayName\": null,\n      \"statusChangedAt\": null,\n      \"statusSource\": null,\n      \"statusActorKind\": null,\n      \"staleOutcome\": \"current\",\n      \"staleCheckedAt\": null,\n      \"staleCheckedCodeVersionId\": null,\n      \"clientId\": \"92113e1ff12fb23e96ac595ea02dfc88\",\n      \"clientIdHash\": \"55ee779df4a2cdc2743c9665d1001844ffa8f57bd7294b257cfed41d2c94c386\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:03:26.640Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:03:26.640Z\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"id\": \"01M246JW5HVBK6B681KM1TTT6G\",\n        \"reviewCommentId\": \"01M246JW5HX5Z39W4H1DPQ3AF0\",\n        \"codeVersionId\": \"01M246JW4YTXCZ0CV7YP2YKGHD\",\n        \"granularity\": \"line\",\n        \"filePath\": \"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go\",\n        \"startLine\": 374,\n        \"startColumn\": null,\n        \"endLine\": null,\n        \"endColumn\": null,\n        \"selectedText\": \"\\t\\t\\tcontinue\",\n        \"nearbyText\": null,\n        \"language\": null\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hasMore\": false,\n  \"nextOffset\": null,\n  \"eventCursor\": \"15\"\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io/api/v1/schemas/ReviewCommentsListResponseBody.json\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"01M246JW5HX5Z39W4H1DPQ3AF0\",\n      \"trailId\": \"01M2464KM3DMQYQ7WVMHE637R0\",\n      \"repositoryId\": \"01KSFAN13YPQ0EWBV5KRE7F5HV\",\n      \"reviewId\": \"01M246JW549DF3JEP3VJ79XJPW\",\n      \"codeVersionId\": \"01M246JW4YTXCZ0CV7YP2YKGHD\",\n      \"actorId\": \"agent:trail-review\",\n      \"actorDisplayName\": null,\n      \"body\": \"When `record.TranscriptUnavailable` is true, this branch appends `payload` (built from `record.AgentID` at line 363) and `continue`s *before* the `record.AgentID == \\\"\\\" || validation.ValidateAgentID(record.AgentID) != nil` guard at line 400 runs. That guard exists specifically, per this function's own doc comment above, to stop an unsafe `AgentID` from reaching `writeTaskRecordEntries` in `checkpoint/persistent.go`, which unconditionally re-validates `task.AgentID` and returns a hard `fmt.Errorf` on failure. That error propagates out of `applySessionWrite` and fails the *entire* checkpoint write (not just this task), directly violating the stated invariant that \\\"a poisoned record produces zero payloads, not an error.\\\" The `TranscriptUnavailable` short-circuit should validate `record.AgentID` the same way before appending, or fall through to the existing check below.\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"statusReason\": null,\n      \"statusActorId\": null,\n      \"statusActorDisplayName\": null,\n      \"statusChangedAt\": null,\n      \"statusSource\": null,\n      \"statusActorKind\": null,\n      \"staleOutcome\": \"current\",\n      \"staleCheckedAt\": null,\n      \"staleCheckedCodeVersionId\": null,\n      \"clientId\": \"92113e1ff12fb23e96ac595ea02dfc88\",\n      \"clientIdHash\": \"55ee779df4a2cdc2743c9665d1001844ffa8f57bd7294b257cfed41d2c94c386\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:03:26.640Z\",\n      \"updatedAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:03:26.640Z\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"id\": \"01M246JW5HVBK6B681KM1TTT6G\",\n        \"reviewCommentId\": \"01M246JW5HX5Z39W4H1DPQ3AF0\",\n        \"codeVersionId\": \"01M246JW4YTXCZ0CV7YP2YKGHD\",\n        \"granularity\": \"line\",\n        \"filePath\": \"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go\",\n        \"startLine\": 374,\n        \"startColumn\": null,\n        \"endLine\": null,\n        \"endColumn\": null,\n        \"selectedText\": \"\\