e/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-321-// then removed from session state by the caller (see resetCheckpointWindow);\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-322-// an in-flight record's transcript-so-far is stored and the record stays so\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-323-// the next condensation re-materializes it. A record whose transcript cannot\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:324:// be resolved or read still produces a payload — with TranscriptUnavailableReason\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-325-// set instead of a Transcript — so the pointer is never silently dropped.\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-326-//\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-327-// A record with an unsafe or empty ToolUseID, or one whose AgentID is unsafe\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-328-// or empty at the point a transcript would be written, is skipped entirely —\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-329-// no payload at all, not even a reason-only one: an unsafe ToolUseID has no\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-330-// safe tasks/<id>/ directory to put a task.json under in the first place, and\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-331-// an empty/unsafe AgentID would corrupt the agent-<id>.jsonl filename (see\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-332-// writeTaskRecordEntries, which re-validates as a last resort). This must\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:333:// never wedge condensation — a poisoned record produces zero payloads, not an\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-334-// error, and the caller's normal completed-record removal\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go-335-// (resetCheckpointWindow) still drops it once completed, since a record that\ncmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.