{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T23:13:38.372Z","ordinal":13451,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08861-a963-7db3-b7f4-840a0a3e6fdf","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1e820413c87d08ffc3d7f16935ffc","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The finding identifies a control-flow bug: validation exists, but its placement means one return path never executes it.\n- The cleanest fix is not duplicate validation inside the fast path; it is to validate both identifiers before constructing any payload.\n- Extending the existing “poisoned record does not wedge condensation” test avoids a new test scaffold and directly pins the invariant already documented by the function.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1788995616386,"completed_at_ms":1788995618372}}
