{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T23:36:18.974Z","ordinal":13651,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cd19a3be99e9a99016aa1ed71f36c87d096d386f88a77a21c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_5PpixgABKiS9kpYHt1cI0zkw","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"entire api --help\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 5000\n});\ntext(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08861-a963-7db3-b7f4-840a0a3e6fdf","create_time":1788996976.906682}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-09T23:36:19.067Z","ordinal":13652,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a06465-c2da-73f2-a18c-e3568bc720c2","turn_id":"01a08861-a963-7db3-b7f4-840a0a3e6fdf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3b8e0395-1c0c-43e3-b659-2981978865da","process_id":"52529","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","entire api --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/subagents","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire api --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Make an authenticated HTTP request to an Entire API and print the JSON response.\n\nThese endpoints are internal and can change shape without notice; where a\npurpose-built command exists, its output is the stable interface.\n\nThe CLI attaches the right bearer token and dials the right host for the\nchosen backend, so you don't have to plumb auth yourself:\n\n  --to core   the control plane (default): orgs, repos, mirrors, clusters, /me\n  --to cell   your home entire-api cell: /me/* activity, repo aggregates\n\nUse --jurisdiction <slug> (e.g. us, eu) to reach a specific jurisdiction's\nentire-api cell instead of your home one; it implies --to cell.\n\n<path> is the full path on that host, e.g. /api/v1/clusters. These\nplaceholders are filled from the current repo's origin remote:\n  {owner} {repo}   the GitHub owner / repo\n  {repo_id}        the repo's Entire ULID (from its mirror) — cells key on this\n\nThe method is GET unless a field/body is given (then POST); override with -X.\n\nUsage:\n  entire api <path> [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire api /api/v1/clusters\n  entire api --to cell /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --jurisdiction eu /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --to cell \"/api/v1/me/recap?repo={repo_id}\"\n  entire api -X POST /api/v1/projects -f name=demo\n\nFlags:\n  -F, --field stringArray       add a typed parameter in key=value format; true/false/null/numbers are converted (repeatable)\n  -H, --header stringArray      add a request header in key:value format (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                    help for api\n  -i, --include                 print the response status line and headers too\n      --input string            file with the request body (\"-\" for stdin)\n  -j, --jurisdiction string     target a specific jurisdiction's cell (e.g. us, eu) instead of your home cell; implies --to cell\n  -X, --method string           HTTP method (default GET, or POST when a field/body is given)\n  -f, --raw-field stringArray   add a string parameter in key=value format (repeatable)\n      --to string               which backend to call: core or cell (default \"core\")\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Make an authenticated HTTP request to an Entire API and print the JSON response.\n\nThese endpoints are internal and can change shape without notice; where a\npurpose-built command exists, its output is the stable interface.\n\nThe CLI attaches the right bearer token and dials the right host for the\nchosen backend, so you don't have to plumb auth yourself:\n\n  --to core   the control plane (default): orgs, repos, mirrors, clusters, /me\n  --to cell   your home entire-api cell: /me/* activity, repo aggregates\n\nUse --jurisdiction <slug> (e.g. us, eu) to reach a specific jurisdiction's\nentire-api cell instead of your home one; it implies --to cell.\n\n<path> is the full path on that host, e.g. /api/v1/clusters. These\nplaceholders are filled from the current repo's origin remote:\n  {owner} {repo}   the GitHub owner / repo\n  {repo_id}        the repo's Entire ULID (from its mirror) — cells key on this\n\nThe method is GET unless a field/body is given (then POST); override with -X.\n\nUsage:\n  entire api <path> [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entir