tID` from reaching `writeTaskRecordEntries` in `checkpoint/persistent.go`, which unconditionally re-validates `task.AgentID` and returns a hard `fmt.Errorf` on failure. That error propagates out of `applySessionWrite` and fails the *entire* checkpoint write (not just this task), directly violating the stated invariant that \\\"a poisoned record produces zero payloads, not an error.\\\" The `TranscriptUnavailable` short-circuit should validate `record.AgentID` the same way before appending, or fall through to the existing check below.\",\n  \"severity\": \"high\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"status\": \"resolved\",\n  \"statusReason\": \"Validated AgentID before all task payload paths, including transcript-unavailable records; regression coverage and mise run check passed.\",\n  \"statusActorId\": \"01KSPWEZWS89N7M7Y97XMXP6JV\",\n  \"statusActorDisplayName\": \"peyton-alt\",\n  \"statusChangedAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:36:37.746Z\",\n  \"statusSource\": \"comment_patch\",\n  \"statusActorKind\": \"human\",\n  \"staleOutcome\": \"current\",\n  \"staleCheckedAt\": null,\n  \"staleCheckedCodeVersionId\": null,\n  \"clientId\": \"92113e1ff12fb23e96ac595ea02dfc88\",\n  \"clientIdHash\": \"55ee779df4a2cdc2743c9665d1001844ffa8f57bd7294b257cfed41d2c94c386\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:03:26.640Z\",\n  \"updatedAt\": \"2026-09-09T23:36:37.746Z\",\n  \"location\": {\n    \"id\": \"01M246JW5HVBK6B681KM1TTT6G\",\n    \"reviewCommentId\": \"01M246JW5HX5Z39W4H1DPQ3AF0\",\n    \"codeVersionId\": \"01M246JW4YTXCZ0CV7YP2YKGHD\",\n    \"granularity\": \"line\",\n    \"filePath\": \"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go\",\n    \"startLine\": 374,\n    \"startColumn\": null,\n    \"endLine\": null,\n    \"endColumn\": null,\n    \"selectedText\": \"\\t\\t\\tcontinue\",\n    \"nearbyText\": null,\n    \"language\": null\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://aws-us-east-2.api.entire.io/api/v1/schemas/ReviewCommentJSON.json\",\n  \"id\